e flow in the Robinhood app) and web_upgrade_url when they are on desktop/web (opens in a browser). If the device is unknown, offer both, clearly labeled "on your phone" vs "on desktop/web". Name the account by its nickname and last four digits (from get_accounts) in the prose, but send the chosen URL exactly as returned with the account number unmasked (masking the number in the link breaks it). If the user reports that neither link works, give them the manual path from upgrade_fallback. The user completes the upgrade themselves in that flow (identity verification and agreement acceptance); this tool never changes the account, so once they confirm they finished, re-fetch get_accounts because the account type from any earlier call is now stale."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:dad5750fbe5bebb263946d946d9bdbbcb271bde43b0ee478d9ca568316834e8c","contract_hash":"sha256:bf8eb32a40fa961b1e3702d22ae01e689e7a27a344b6764f61b069bdcfd4d450"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Account-setting and upgrade flows are outside the allowed read and equity-order mappings.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_limited_margin_upgrade_info","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Account-setting and upgrade flows are outside the allowed read and equity-order mappings.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_option_chains":{"contract":{"name":"get_option_chains","title":null,"description":"List option chains for one or more underlyings. A chain describes the full set of expiration dates and contracts for a given underlying. One of underlying_symbol or ids is required.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ids":{"type":"string","description":"Comma-separated chain UUIDs."},"underlying_symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Ticker filter; covers equity and index underlyings (e.g. 'AAPL', 'SPX')."}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"chains":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Chain UUID; pass to get_option_instruments as chain_id."},"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Chain ticker (may differ from underlying — e.g. 'SPX' for an index chain)."},"can_open_position":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether new positions can be opened on this chain."},"cash_component":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Cash component for adjusted chains; null when none."},"expiration_dates":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"All available expirations (YYYY-MM-DD)."},"trade_value_multiplier":{"type":"string","description":"Contract multiplier; typically '100'."},"underlying_instruments":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"instrument":{"type":"string","description":"Underlying equity instrument URL."},"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Underlying equity ticker."}},"required":["instrument","symbol"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Underlying equity instruments. Empty for index chains."},"min_ticks":{"type":"object","properties":{"above_tick":{"type":"string","description":"Minimum price increment above cutoff_price."},"below_tick":{"type":"string","description":"Minimum price increment below cutoff_price."},"cutoff_price":{"type":"string","description":"Price boundary between the below/above tick regimes."}},"description":"Tick-size rules.","required":["above_tick","below_tick","cutoff_price"],"additionalProperties":false},"late_close_state":{"type":"string","description":"Late-close state; 'enabled' adds 15 minutes of trading after the regular close."},"extended_hours_state":{"type":"string","description":"'enabled' or 'disabled'. CURB market_hours values require 'enabled' AND an index chain."},"settle_on_open":{"type":"boolean","description":"True for AM-settled expirations, false for PM. When an underlying has multiple chains, they may not split cleanly by AM/PM — check per chain."},"sellout_time_to_expiration":{"type":"integer","description":"Seconds before expiration when Robinhood begins force-closing positions on this chain. Always 0 for index options — sellout does not apply to index chains."}},"required":["id","symbol","can_open_position","cash_component","expiration_dates","trade_value_multiplier","underlying_instruments","min_ticks","late_close_state","extended_hours_state","settle_on_open","sellout_time_to_expiration"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Option chains matching the filter. Empty when nothing resolves."},"next":{"type":"string","description":"Next-page URL. Empty when there are no more pages."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["chains"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Pass id to get_option_instruments as chain_id to list contracts. CURB market_hours on place_option_order require extended_hours_state='enabled' AND an index chain (underlying_instruments empty). When the user mentions AM/PM/morning/evening expiration, check settle_on_open per chain — same underlying can have multiple chains, so do not assume they split cleanly by settlement. Present id, symbol, expiration_dates (annotate AM when settle_on_open is true), and trade_value_multiplier."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:34dacd0762ce625bf8f94420ebeae3a66a45b52629d53344c22bf505a30820cf","contract_hash":"sha256:e150c6fc18546a66a2b99c65971cca6f81cf5bb977db1105f71f4e78a13d6b9f"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_option_chains","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_option_historicals":{"contract":{"name":"get_option_historicals","title":null,"description":"Get OHLC price bars for one or more option contracts (by instrument UUID) across an explicit time range. Use this for charting an option's price history and "recent activity" questions. The server auto-selects an interval when one is not provided. If the bar's interpolated field is true, bar was synthesized to fill a gap and carry no new information.

Parameter rules:
- instrument_ids are option contract UUIDs from get_option_instruments. Resolve underlying -> get_option_chains -> get_option_instruments first; this tool does not accept ticker symbols.
- interval is optional; when omitted the server auto-selects an interval that targets a bounded bar count across the range. Provide an explicit interval only when you need a specific granularity.
- bounds defaults to 'regular' (regular hours). Use '24_5'/'24_7' only when the user explicitly asks about extended-hours or overnight option activity.
- If an explicitly requested interval would produce more bars than the upstream allows for the range, the call is rejected — narrow the range or coarsen the interval. The cap does not apply when interval is auto-selected.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"instrument_ids":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Option contract instrument UUIDs (from get_option_instruments). Up to 10 per call."},"start_time":{"type":"string","description":"Start of the range (RFC3339 UTC, e.g. '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'). Required."},"end_time":{"type":"string","description":"End of the range (RFC3339 UTC). Optional — when omitted, defaults to the current time."},"interval":{"type":"string","description":"Bar interval. Optional — when omitted, the server auto-selects an interval that targets a bounded bar count across the range. Intraday: 15second, 30second, minute, 5minute, 10minute, 30minute, hour, 4hour. Interday: day, week, month, 3month, 6month, year, 5year, 10year, 20year, 50year. Note: the 1-minute bar is named 'minute' (not '1minute')."},"bounds":{"type":"string","description":"Session bounds. One of 'regular' (regular hours, default), '24_5', or '24_7'. Use '24_5'/'24_7' only when the user explicitly asks about extended-hours or overnight option activity (index options, and certain equity options)."}},"required":["instrument_ids","start_time"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"instrument_id":{"type":"string","description":"UUID of the option contract."},"occ_symbol":{"type":"string","description":"OCC-format contract symbol, e.g. 'AAPL  260116C00150000'."},"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Underlying root symbol, e.g. 'AAPL'."},"interval":{"type":"string","description":"Bar interval. Echoes the request when one was supplied; otherwise the server-selected value."},"bounds":{"type":"string","description":"Session bounds echoed from the request."},"bars":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"begins_at":{"type":"string","description":"Start of the bar (RFC3339 UTC). Bars are left-edge labeled."},"open_price":{"type":"string","description":"First price in the bar, as a decimal string."},"high_price":{"type":"string","description":"Highest price in the bar, as a decimal string."},"low_price":{"type":"string","description":"Lowest price in the bar, as a decimal string."},"close_price":{"type":"string","description":"Last price in the bar, as a decimal string. NOT the official settled close; for that use get_option_quotes."},"session":{"type":"string","description":"Wire-format session of the bar: 'reg' (regular hours), 'pre' (pre-market), 'post' (after-hours), or 'overnight' (index-option overnight). Empty when no session applies."},"interpolated":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the bar was synthesized to fill a gap (no trades occurred); its OHLC values are forward-filled from a nearby bar and carry no new information."}},"required":["begins_at","open_price","high_price","low_price","close_price","session"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Bars in ascending time order. May be empty if no trading activity in the window."}},"required":["instrument_id","occ_symbol","symbol","interval","bounds","bars"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"One entry per requested contract that resolved upstream, in request order. Empty if no instrument_id resolved."},"not_found":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Requested instrument_ids that did not resolve (invalid, expired, or unknown). Absent when every requested id resolved."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Bars are left-edge labeled in UTC; convert to the user's timezone for presentation. Treat interpolated=true bars as gap-fill — they carry no new information and should usually be hidden in charts and ignored for analytics. Option bars carry no volume. close_price on the most recent bar is NOT the official settled close — use get_option_quotes for the current mark and the official prior-session close. For a multi-bar move, compute the return from the first bar's open_price to the last bar's close_price. Each entry in results is keyed by instrument_id; requested ids that did not resolve are listed in not_found. When the request omitted interval, the 'interval' field on each result reports what the server auto-selected."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:5ba439e92edc65384354013c00d2a57668d432d7d7b0f1f52770a5b746f7e5a3","contract_hash":"sha256:0cf0966ec8ce67aede9d47314fcb78496c48034de41d2f31bbd1f9b1d991b2fa"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_option_historicals","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_option_instruments":{"contract":{"name":"get_option_instruments","title":null,"description":"List option contracts. One of chain_symbol, chain_id, or ids is required; narrow further with expiration_dates, strike_price, type, state. When looking up contracts for a specific expiration, call this in parallel for every chain whose expiration_dates (from get_option_chains) includes the date. For AM/PM/morning/evening preferences, first check settle_on_open on each chain via get_option_chains and only query matching chains.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"chain_id":{"type":"string","description":"Chain UUID."},"chain_symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Underlying ticker (e.g. 'AAPL')."},"expiration_dates":{"type":"string","description":"Comma-separated YYYY-MM-DD expirations."},"strike_price":{"type":"string","description":"Exact strike (e.g. '150.0000')."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"'call' or 'put'."},"state":{"type":"string","description":"'active' (default), 'expired', or 'inactive'. Use 'expired' to find option contracts whose expiration date has passed; 'inactive' is for delisted/withdrawn contracts that never expired."},"tradability":{"type":"string","description":"'tradable' or 'untradable' (untradable is rejected at the tool layer)."},"ids":{"type":"string","description":"Comma-separated instrument UUIDs."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"Pagination cursor. Omit for the first page; for the next page, pass the cursor query param from the prior response's next URL."}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"instruments":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Option instrument UUID; reference this in an order's legs."},"chain_id":{"type":"string","description":"Owning option chain UUID."},"chain_symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Underlying ticker (e.g. 'AAPL')."},"underlying_type":{"type":"string","description":"'equity' or 'index'. Matches the underlying_type filter on get_option_orders / get_option_positions."},"expiration_date":{"type":"string","description":"YYYY-MM-DD contract expiration."},"sellout_datetime":{"type":"string","description":"ISO 8601 timestamp at which Robinhood may force-close a position in this contract. Authoritative answer — handles index/equity, AM/PM settle, late-close, and T-1 logic per contract."},"strike_price":{"type":"string","description":"Contract strike."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"'call' or 'put'."},"state":{"type":"string","description":"'active' (tradable), 'expired' (past expiration date), or 'inactive' (delisted/withdrawn before expiration)."},"tradability":{"type":"string","description":"'tradable' or 'untradable'; active contracts may still be untradable near expiration or during halts."},"trade_value_multiplier":{"type":"string","description":"Multiplier converting a per-contract price to a total dollar amount: price × quantity × this. '100' for standard contracts; a corporate action can change it. Not a share count."},"min_ticks":{"type":"object","properties":{"above_tick":{"type":"string","description":"Minimum price increment above cutoff_price."},"below_tick":{"type":"string","description":"Minimum price increment below cutoff_price."},"cutoff_price":{"type":"string","description":"Price boundary between the below/above tick regimes."}},"description":"Tick-size rules.","required":["above_tick","below_tick","cutoff_price"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["id","chain_id","chain_symbol","underlying_type","expiration_date","sellout_datetime","strike_price","type","state","tradability","trade_value_multiplier","min_ticks"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Option contracts matching the filter. Empty when none match."},"next":{"type":"string","description":"Next-page URL. Empty when there are no more pages."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["instruments"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Present chain_symbol, expiration_date, type, strike_price; flag state when not 'active' or tradability when not 'tradable'. Pass id to an order's leg.option_id. Quote sellout_datetime when the user asks "when will Robinhood force-close this position?" — it is the authoritative per-contract timestamp covering equity/index, AM/PM settle, and T-1 logic. underlying_type ('equity' or 'index') is informational; mention only when it affects strategy. When next is non-null, extract the cursor query param and call this tool again."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:482e781369ccee0590f952670305efe6e1bd6dd2e53e2e4b0b78654b3a0739ca","contract_hash":"sha256:b106017b42787c5f6fe66eb64e38bb6815308323ba4175ef14a4fa17b5d66cd7"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_option_instruments","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_option_level_upgrade_info":{"contract":{"name":"get_option_level_upgrade_info","title":null,"description":"Get the upgrade URL to apply for — or raise — options access on an account. The returned link routes the customer into the correct application for their target tier, including upgrading an existing option_level_2 account to option_level_3. Call when the user requests an options level their account doesn't yet have: option_level_2 enables long calls/puts, covered calls, and cash-secured puts; option_level_3 adds spreads and other multi-leg/complex strategies. option_level_3 additionally requires a margin or limited-margin account. If the account type is cash, do NOT call this tool for an L3 request — the customer must first switch to a margin/limited-margin account via get_limited_margin_upgrade_info, then re-fetch get_accounts; call this tool for L3 only once the account type is margin or limited margin. option_level_2 has no account-type requirement and is available on cash accounts. Map the user's requested strategy to its required level and call this tool if the account is below it — null/empty/option_level_0 for any options, or option_level_2 for an L3-only strategy such as a spread. Do NOT call when the account already has the required level or higher.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Brokerage account number to generate the upgrade URL for. Obtain from get_accounts."}},"required":["account_number"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"upgrade_url":{"type":"string","description":"Direct link to apply for options access. Present this to the user as a tappable link."},"account_number":{"type":"string","description":"The account this upgrade URL applies to."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["upgrade_url","account_number"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Send the upgrade_url to the user as a tappable link. The user must click the link, complete the full options application flow, and get approved. Once the user confirms they have been successfully approved: call get_accounts immediately with a fresh request. Do not use any option_level value from a previous get_accounts call — that data is stale until re-fetched. The option_level field on the new get_accounts response will confirm the new access level. If you do not yet have the account_number, call get_accounts first."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:417f0dc43bd9a7a7223549b512d53b38cf87d0b0b1619979ec3e768f7f0e9111","contract_hash":"sha256:482c972bbed75341b36a685c3b316d82c7f155914fac23e3ac09d6bdf2b141ba"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options and account-setting flows are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_option_level_upgrade_info","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options and account-setting flows are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_option_orders":{"contract":{"name":"get_option_orders","title":null,"description":"Fetch options orders for an account — list mode (newest first; open and closed, including fills, cancellations, and rejections) or single-order mode by passing order_id. When the user asks for "orders" without specifying equity or options, call both get_option_orders and get_equity_orders in parallel.

Filtering tips:
- Prefer narrow queries: combine state and/or created_at_gte for specific questions — the per-page cap is fixed.
- chain_ids filters by underlying chain UUID (from get_option_chains).
