still working?'."},"time_in_force":{"type":"string","description":"'gtc' (good till canceled), 'gfd' (good for day), 'ioc' (immediate or cancel), 'gfw' (good for week), 'gfm' (good for month)."},"quantity":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Originally-requested asset quantity. On dollar-based orders the server derives it at placement: from the quote for market and from the stop price for stop_loss (treat those as estimated until fills confirm them), and from the limit price for limit/stop_limit (exact at placement)."},"cumulative_quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Total asset quantity filled so far. Less than quantity while partially filled; equal once filled."},"canceled_quantity":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Quantity that was canceled before fill (only populated on partial-fill-then-cancel paths)."},"price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Order price (interpretation depends on type — limit price for limit; for stop_loss it is the collared worst-case execution bound, NOT the trigger, which lives in stop_price; for market it is the raw quote side-price on a preview_crypto_order response — the same price the app displays, NOT collared — but the collared worst-case execution bound on placed orders; stablecoin pairs are never collared, so their preview and placed prices both carry the raw quote). Use limit_price / stop_price for the unambiguous fields."},"limit_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Limit price for limit / stop_limit orders. Null for market / stop_loss."},"stop_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Stop trigger price for stop_loss / stop_limit orders. Null for market / limit."},"average_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Volume-weighted average fill price across executions. Null until the first fill."},"entered_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Price the user originally entered (pre-collaring). Different from limit_price after server-side collaring adjusts the order."},"rounded_executed_notional":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Total notional filled so far in the quote currency, rounded to 2 decimals."},"executions":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Execution UUID."},"price":{"type":"string","description":"Reported fill price per unit asset (e.g. USD per BTC). For the price the user actually paid after venue adjustments, use effective_price."},"effective_price":{"type":"string","description":"Per-unit price after venue fees or price adjustments are applied — closer to the user's realized fill economics than price."},"quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Asset quantity filled in this execution."},"notional":{"type":"string","description":"effective_price * quantity, rounded to 2 decimals where applicable."},"exchange_name":{"type":"string","description":"Routing venue name. Treat as informational; do not surface unless the user asks about routing."},"timestamp":{"type":"string","description":"When the fill occurred (UTC)."}},"required":["id","price","effective_price","quantity","notional","timestamp"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Per-fill detail. Reference for per-execution timing or price questions; for headline 'what did this fill at?' use average_price."},"initiator_type":{"type":"string","description":"Source that placed the order: 'api_trading', 'trading_view', 'recurring', 'paycheck', 'rh_assistant', 'agentic_trading' (when nummus adds that enum value), or one of the internal crypto-specific values. Tells the user whether they placed this order via app, API, recurring buy, or an agent."},"speculative":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the order was created as a speculative pre-trade check (no upstream side effect). Should always be false on real placed orders; populated read-only by upstream."},"created_at":{"type":"string","description":"When the order was created (UTC)."},"updated_at":{"type":"string","description":"Last server-side state update (UTC) — fill, cancel, reject, etc."},"canceled_at":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"When the cancel was acknowledged. Null when the order has not been canceled."},"routing":{"type":"string","description":"How the order is routed for execution. Present verbatim as the routing line item; absent when routing information is unavailable."},"rounded_estimated_notional_with_estimated_fee":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Estimated total cost (buy) or net proceeds (sell) in the quote currency, with ONLY the estimated fee already included. It does NOT include any additional taxes or deductions."},"rounded_uncollared_estimated_notional_with_estimated_fee":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Same as rounded_estimated_notional_with_estimated_fee but before price collaring. Null when collaring does not apply."},"rounded_executed_notional_with_fee":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Notional actually executed so far only including fees without netting additional taxes, in the quote currency. Grows as fills come in; 0 before the first fill. For the executed figure net of all taxes and fees use net_rounded_executed_notional."},"total_executed_notional":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Total executed notional so far only including fees without netting additional taxes. Null until there are fills."},"net_rounded_estimated_notional":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Estimated total cost (buy) or credit (sell) net of ALL taxes and fees. On a preview, present this as the estimated total cost or credit line item alongside the separate estimated_fee value. Never subtract the fee or taxes from it again. Null when an order has fills."},"net_rounded_executed_notional":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Executed total cost (buy) or credit (sell) net of ALL taxes and fees — the definitive amount actually debited or credited. Null before the first fill. Grows as fills come in. Never subtract the fee or any taxes from it again."},"fees":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"fee_structure":{"type":"string","description":"How the fee was computed (e.g. a fixed percentage or a volume-tiered rate)."},"fee_data":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"fee_type":{"type":"string","description":"Fee category (e.g. a transaction/spread fee)."},"fee_amount":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Fee amount in the quote currency (USD)."},"fee_ratio":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Rate this fee was computed at, when applicable."}},"description":"This fee's amount, type, and rate.","additionalProperties":false}},"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Itemized fee breakdown for exchange-routed orders. Empty or absent when the order carries no itemized fees."},"tax_withholding":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"withholding_rate":{"type":"string","description":"Withholding rate preformatted as a percent (e.g. '24%'), aggregated across the federal and any state portion. Print verbatim. Absent when no rate is available."},"estimated_withholding_amount":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Estimated USD to be withheld from this sell's proceeds. Present only while cumulative_quantity is 0. Exactly one of this and total_withholding_amount is ever present, so read the one that is there."},"total_withholding_amount":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Actual USD withheld from proceeds across fills so far (final once fully filled). Present only once cumulative_quantity is positive. Exactly one of this and estimated_withholding_amount is ever present, so read the one that is there."}},"description":"Backup withholding on this sell order's proceeds. Present only when withholding applies (sell orders for subject users; never on IRA accounts) — when absent, do not mention withholding. amount and withholding_rate are the display-ready figure and percent.","additionalProperties":false}},"description":"Transient preview of the order — same shape as a placed order (get_crypto_orders results), with estimated cost/credit and fees resolved. No order was placed; id and lifecycle fields are not meaningful.","required":["id","account_id","currency_pair_id","side","type","state","time_in_force","quantity","cumulative_quantity","created_at","updated_at"],"additionalProperties":false},"fee_rate":{"type":"string","description":"Rate the estimated fee was computed at, preformatted: the bare percent on single-rate fee pricing (e.g. '0.35%'), suffixed with the liquidity role on maker/taker-priced accounts (e.g. '0.05% maker', '0.1% taker'). Absent when no fee rate applies to this order."},"estimated_fee":{"type":"string","description":"Estimated fee for this order in USD. 0 when no fee applies to this order. The estimated total cost already includes this fee — never add them together or annotate the total with it."},"fee_context":{"type":"string","description":"Why no fee rate applies to this order even though the account trades with fee pricing, preformatted for display (e.g. 'asset not eligible for fee tiers'). Only ever present when fee_rate is absent; absent when no explanation applies."},"crypto_account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Crypto account number the order is previewed against. Present THIS as the account to the user — not the brokerage account number used to look the account up. When absent, refer to the account as the user's linked crypto account."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["order","estimated_fee"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"This tool does NOT place the order — it returns a preview for the user to review. Present the preview as a table with exactly these rows, in this order: 1) side; 2) asset — symbol and pair, e.g. DOGE (DOGE-USD); 3) order type — ALWAYS the app's name: stop_loss = "stop order", stop_limit = "stop limit order"; never show the raw stop_loss/stop_limit values to the user; 4) quantity — always phrased as an amount of the asset (e.g. '0.001542 ETH'), never as 'shares'; for orders entered by quantity, the exact amount the user specified (for market and stop_loss label the per-unit price as estimated); for orders entered by dollar_amount, include the per-unit price (for market the response's price — the raw quote, the same price the app displays — with quantity derivation described under dollar_amount; the stop price for stop_loss, the limit price for limit/stop_limit) — label the quantity estimated for market and stop_loss, and exact for limit and stop_limit (derived deterministically from the limit price at placement); 5) limit price (limit and stop_limit orders only); 6) stop price (stop orders only); 7) notional entered (only when the resolved amount differs from what the user asked for); 8) time in force; 9) estimated fee — from estimated_fee, shown even when 0, with the fee_rate value appended verbatim in parentheses when present, e.g. "$1.23 (0.5% maker)" or "$1.23 (0.35%)"; when fee_rate is absent and fee_context is present, append the fee_context value verbatim in parentheses instead, e.g. "$0 (asset not eligible for fee tiers)" — never re-derive, re-label, or reword either parenthetical, and no parenthetical when both are absent; 10) estimated backup withholding — include this row ONLY when the order's tax_withholding is present, from tax_withholding.estimated_withholding_amount (the only amount a preview carries — it has no fills), labeled "Estimated backup withholding", with the tax_withholding.withholding_rate value appended verbatim in parentheses when present, e.g. "$23.88 (24%)"; never raise withholding at all when tax_withholding is absent; 11) estimated total cost or credit — from the order's net_rounded_estimated_notional, which is ALREADY net of both the fee in row 9 and the withholding in row 10, so present it as the bottom line and never subtract either row from it again; if it is absent, omit this row rather than substituting any other field as the total; label it plainly without qualifiers like "(fee included)"; ignore order.rounded_estimated_notional_with_estimated_fee, which is net of the fee only and will overstate a withholding-subject sell; a limit buy's final debit never exceeds it, a market buy's final debit is typically ~it with a worst case up to the collar more, a market sell's credit is typically ~it with a worst case up to the collar less, a stop order's fill notional is typically ~it with a worst case up to the collar worse; mention the collar sizing (see dollar_amount) only when the user asks why it is estimated; 12) routing. Directly below the table, add this line verbatim: "You can switch between Market Maker Routing and Exchange Routing anytime in the Robinhood app under Settings → Crypto → Fee Tiers." — omit it only when the routing row is absent. When tax_withholding is present, add this sentence verbatim directly below the table: "Your order will be subject to backup withholding. Please confirm your tax status at https://robinhood.com/tax-certification." — exactly as written, no rewording; omit it entirely when tax_withholding is absent. Identify the account by the crypto_account_number returned in the response, not by the brokerage account number the tool was called with. A request for a 'stop loss', 'stop order', or 'stop market' order is the stop_loss type — do not ask which stop type (a limit price given alongside the trigger makes it stop_limit); ask only when the phrasing names no type, e.g. a bare 'stop' or 'protect my position'. Then get explicit user confirmation before calling place_crypto_order. No order was created and no id was assigned; the response mirrors an order but is transient."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:499c41da57c3ec2583d7c5d5f0fa34380b64622645c119cedda500bdfeda504d","contract_hash":"sha256:99f523a0f4d31672d097b66a91ed2f8d1df0d3d2689684a2c1222c67ac75771e"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto orders are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"preview_crypto_order","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto orders are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"remove_from_watchlist":{"contract":{"name":"remove_from_watchlist","title":null,"description":"Remove items from a watchlist. Exactly one of symbols (stocks/ETFs), currency_pair_ids (crypto), or index_ids (market indexes) is required — mutually exclusive. For options use remove_option_from_watchlist. Items not on the list are no-ops (not errors). Confirm with the user before calling.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"list_id":{"type":"string","description":"UUID of the watchlist to remove items from."},"symbols":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Stock symbols to remove (e.g. ['AAPL']). Mutually exclusive with currency_pair_ids and index_ids."},"currency_pair_ids":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Currency-pair UUIDs to remove. Mutually exclusive with symbols and index_ids."},"index_ids":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Index UUIDs to remove. Mutually exclusive with symbols and currency_pair_ids."}},"required":["list_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"symbols":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"The stock symbols this call targeted (instrument path)."},"currency_pair_ids":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"The currency-pair UUIDs this call targeted (crypto path)."},"index_ids":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"The index UUIDs this call targeted (index path)."},"object_type":{"type":"string","description":"'instrument' when symbols were used, 'currency_pair' when currency_pair_ids were used, 'index' when index_ids were used."},"list_id":{"type":"string","description":"The watchlist this call targeted."},"operation":{"type":"string","description":"'create' for add_to_watchlist, 'delete' for remove_from_watchlist."},"status":{"type":"string","description":"'ok' when the upstream accepted the operation."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["object_type","list_id","operation","status"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"On success the response echoes the operations applied. 404 means the list_id is not writable by the user."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:49b18f1e7eb128e843373f18992173d8239fca2c49b12878ad7cc404848f08be","contract_hash":"sha256:a5c626c1bd0851d561cb8ef02e3b31787ef179fff9d0b4d3cc3101e2db03200b"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Watchlists are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"remove_from_watchlist","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Watchlists are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"remove_option_from_watchlist":{"contract":{"name":"remove_option_from_watchlist","title":null,"description":"Remove option contracts from the user's options watchlist. Specify the same position_type used when the contract was added (defaults to "long"). Contracts not on the list are no-ops. Confirm with the user before calling.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"option_ids":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Option contract UUIDs to remove. The position_type must match how each contract was added (most likely "long")."},"position_type":{"type":"string","description":""long" (default) or "short". Must match how the contract was originally added."}},"required":["option_ids"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"option_ids":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Option contract UUIDs this call targeted, echoed for the caller's reference."},"position_type":{"type":"string","description":"The position_type applied to every contract in this call."},"list_id":{"type":"string","description":"The options watchlist this call resolved to and targeted."},"operation":{"type":"string","description":""create" for add_option_to_watchlist, "delete" for remove_option_from_watchlist."},"status":{"type":"string","description":""ok" when the upstream accepted the operation."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["option_ids","position_type","list_id","operation","status"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Each option_id is matched as a single-leg position with the supplied position_type. The upstream resolves the leg back to the existing strategy and removes it. "no options watchlist found" means the user has not enabled options trading."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:7af51cf9593e8ee9651d539342a1dcc0dad05be1365fa109ea30f0d8282232cb","contract_hash":"sha256:c1b4bfabbf42ef7ac4c90b5baf47d5ce00df68ae0ca37729ea808873c7335e68"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options and watchlists are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"remove_option_from_watchlist","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options and watchlists are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"review_equity_order":{"contract":{"name":"review_equity_order","title":null,"description":"Simulate a stock order without placing it. Returns the current quote plus pre-trade alerts (buying power, PDT, instrument halt, etc.). Call this by default before place_equity_order unless the user has very explicitly asked to skip review. Requires an agentic_allowed=true account; non-agentic accounts are rejected — do not call.

Parameter rules:
- If the user has not specified type, ask. For immediate fills with price protection, prefer a marketable limit at the current ask over a plain market.
- Outside regular hours, only limit orders execute. For an immediate fill during extended or overnight/24-hour sessions, place a limit order (a marketable limit at the current ask) with market_hours set to that session — not a market order. Market and stop orders are regular_hours-only; placed after hours as regular_hours they queue for the next regular open.
- Provide exactly one of quantity or dollar_amount; dollar_amount requires type=market (server computes shares from last_trade_price).
- Fractional shares: only on type=market with market_hours=regular_hours, eligible accounts, up to 6 decimal places, no short sells.
- limit_price required for limit/stop_limit; stop_price required for stop_market/stop_limit.
- Fractional and dollar-based orders only place in regular_hours; the tool rejects them in other sessions.
- tax_lots (specified-lot selling, sell only): to sell specific lots, first call get_equity_tax_lots for the symbol, then pass tax_lots as {open_lot_id, quantity} pairs whose quantities sum to the order quantity. Omit for default (FIFO) cost basis. US accounts only; not allowed with dollar_amount, stop orders, all_day_hours, or fractional limit orders.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Brokerage account number. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts. Must be agentic_allowed=true; non-agentic accounts are rejected."},"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Stock symbol."},"side":{"type":"string","description":"'buy' or 'sell'."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"'market', 'limit', 'stop_market', or 'stop_limit'."},"quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Number of shares. Decimals (fractional) allowed for market + regular_hours only."},"dollar_amount":{"type":"string","description":"USD notional (e.g. '100.00'). Only valid with type=market."},"limit_price":{"type":"string","description":"Limit price; required for limit or stop_limit."},"stop_price":{"type":"string","description":"Stop trigger price; required for stop_market or stop_limit."},"time_in_force":{"type":"string","description":"'gfd' (good for day) or 'gtc' (good till cancelled). Default: gfd."},"market_hours":{"type":"string","description":"'regular_hours' (default, 9:30–16:00 ET), 'extended_hours' (pre-/post-market), or 'all_day_hours' (the 24 Hour Market / overnight session). extended_hours and all_day_hours execute limit orders only — market, stop_market, and stop_limit are regular_hours-only and are rejected if tagged to another session."},"tax_lots":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"open_lot_id":{"type":"string","description":"open_lot_id of the open tax lot to sell, from get_equity_tax_lots."},"quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Shares to sell from this lot as a decimal string; at most the lot's quantity_available."}},"required":["open_lot_id","quantity"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Optional specified-lot selection for a SELL order. To sell specific tax lots instead of the default FIFO cost basis, pass the exact lots as {open_lot_id, quantity} objects, where open_lot_id comes from get_equity_tax_lots and the quantities sum to the order quantity. Omit for default FIFO. Sell only; at most 30 lots; US accounts only. Not allowed with dollar_amount, stop_market/stop_limit, all_day_hours, or fractional-share limit orders."}},"required":["account_number","symbol","side","type"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Echoed symbol."},"side":{"type":"string","description":"Echoed side."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Echoed order type."},"quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Echoed share quantity. Omitted for dollar-based orders."},"dollar_amount":{"type":"string","description":"Echoed dollar amount (USD). Omitted for share-quantity orders."},"limit_price":{"type":"string","description":"Echoed limit price."},"stop_price":{"type":"string","description":"Echoed stop trigger price."},"order_checks":{"type":"object","description":"Pre-trade alert. Empty object {} means no alerts. Non-empty shape: {alert_type: <UPPER_SNAKE_CASE>, <alert_type_lowercase>_alert_details: {...}}. Present alert_type verbatim along with the details — do not enumerate alert types; new ones ship regularly."},"quote_data":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Ticker symbol."},"last_trade_price":{"type":"string","description":"Most recent regular-hours trade (9:30-16:00 ET). Stays frozen at the closing print after the close until the next open; not the official settled close."},"venue_last_trade_time":{"type":"string","description":"Timestamp of last_trade_price."},"last_non_reg_trade_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Most recent pre-market / after-hours / overnight trade. Null during regular hours or when the symbol does not trade in the current session."},"venue_last_non_reg_trade_time":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Timestamp of last_non_reg_trade_price. Reveals which non-regular session the trade came from."},"adjusted_previous_close":{"type":"string","description":"Prior-day close adjusted for splits, dividends, and mergers."},"previous_close":{"type":"string","description":"Raw prior closing print — not corporate-action adjusted and not the official settled close."},"previous_close_date":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"YYYY-MM-DD trading date that previous_close corresponds to. Null for symbols that have never had a settled close."},"bid_price":{"type":"string","description":"Highest current buy-order price. Zero when the book is closed or unavailable."},"venue_bid_time":{"type":"string","description":"Timestamp of bid_price."},"ask_price":{"type":"string","description":"Lowest current sell-order price. Zero when the book is closed or unavailable."},"venue_ask_time":{"type":"string","description":"Timestamp of ask_price."},"has_traded":{"type":"boolean","description":"False for instruments that have never traded; price fields are meaningless when false."},"state":{"type":"string","description":"Instrument listing state — 'active' is normal; other values (inactive, delisted, unlisted) mean the instrument is not in normal trading state."}},"description":"Live market data (single quote); same shape and semantics as get_equity_quotes results[0].quote.","required":["symbol","last_trade_price","venue_last_trade_time","last_non_reg_trade_price","venue_last_non_reg_trade_time","adjusted_previous_close","previous_close","previous_close_date","bid_price","venue_bid_time","ask_price","venue_ask_time","has_traded","state"],"additionalProperties":false},"market_data_disclosure":{"type":"string","description":"Compliance market-data disclosure string (NBBO bid/ask with sizes + venue codes, last trade, and update time), e.g. 'Bid $218.00 × 1400 P · Ask $218.09 × 100 M · Last $218.05 × 100. Updated 1:21 PM ET.'. The update time is rendered in the user's timezone (from the x-timezone-id header, default ET). Display this verbatim to the user. Empty only when live prices were unavailable."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["symbol","side","type","order_checks","quote_data"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"This tool does NOT place the order — it returns a preview for the user to review. Reaching this tool means the user opted into the review step, so you MUST present the preview to the user (symbol, side, type, quantity or dollar_amount, limit/stop prices, estimated execution) and get explicit confirmation before calling place_equity_order. This holds even when order_checks is empty ({}) — empty means no broker alerts, NOT that confirmation can be skipped; the user asked to review, so let them review. Surface any non-empty alert in order_checks verbatim alongside the preview. In addition, you MUST always show the quotes to the user for compliance reasons: whenever market_data_disclosure is present, display it to the user exactly as provided — verbatim and unmodified — as the required compliance quote disclosure. Market orders: estimate execution from quote_data.last_trade_price (ask for buys, bid for sells when spreads are wide). Limit orders: compare limit_price to quote_data bid/ask so the user knows the distance from market."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:e71382d43305c73eab78d4b4e5647cff542fa46e43cc1640077ec426854127c8","contract_hash":"sha256:e9f2a3daee49dcca52b70e34b93692b3e29c5e8965b664e00f0c3505f98871e0"},"category":"order.preflight","arguments":{"account_number":"{account_id}","symbol":"{symbol}","side":"{side}","type":"{order_type}","quantity":"{qty}","limit_price":"{limit_price}","stop_price":"{stop_price}","time_in_force":"{time_in_force}","market_hours":"{extended_hours}"},"result":{},"reason":"This reviews one proposed long-only equity order without placing it.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"review_equity_order","category":"order.preflight","arguments":{"account_number":"{account_id}","symbol":"{symbol}","side":"{side}","type":"{order_type}","quantity":"{qty}","limit_price":"{limit_price}","stop_price":"{stop_price}","time_in_force":"{time_in_force}","market_hours":"{extended_hours}"},"result":{},"reason":"This reviews one proposed long-only equity order without placing it.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"review_option_order":{"contract":{"name":"review_option_order","title":null,"description":"Simulate an options order without placing it. Returns the current quote plus pre-trade alerts. Call this by default before place_option_order or replace_option_order unless the user has very explicitly asked to skip review.

Capability: single-leg options orders — Level 2 strategies (covered calls, cash-secured puts, long calls and puts). Multi-leg spreads (Level 3 strategies) are supported on option_level_3 accounts.

Account requirements: confirm via get_accounts that the chosen account is agentic_allowed=true AND has option_level_2 or option_level_3. If agentic_allowed=false do NOT call. If option_level is empty or option_level_0, do NOT call; follow the get_accounts guide for how to direct the user to enroll.

Parameter rules:
- legs: option_id (from get_option_instruments), side, position_effect, optional ratio_quantity per leg.
- Multi-leg leg layouts — vertical spread: two legs, same expiration, different strikes, opposite sides. Calendar: two legs, same strike, different expirations. Iron condor: four legs, a put spread plus a call spread. Roll: close the leg you hold (position_effect 'close', side opposite the position) plus open the replacement ('open').
- Get the net price from the user rather than inferring it from individual leg quotes.
- Multi-leg is not available on cash or retirement accounts through this tool.
- type: 'limit' (default), 'market', 'stop_limit', 'stop_market'. If unspecified, ask. price for limit/stop_limit; stop_price for stop_market/stop_limit.
- market, stop_market, and stop_limit are single-leg only. market and stop_market are also GFD, regular_hours only. stop_market is sell-to-close only with stop_price below the current ask. Non-limit-immediate types are blocked in any extended-hours session.
