'pending_cancelled' = in flight; 'cancelled' or 'partially_filled_rest_cancelled' = succeeded; any filled state = a fill raced the cancel. Offer to check the final state. On error, the cancel was rejected outright — report verbatim."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:8e4b1d5784426a585c445bd0e5334ad578d3644309ccbf7cd22e7a4154b9534a","contract_hash":"sha256:4cec6376cc80bbdd72ab93974e005483ae59265e677d7b01fb88c2bea21d9dfe"},"category":"order.cancel","arguments":{"account_number":"{account_id}","order_id":"{order_id}"},"result":{"accepted":"data.accepted"},"reason":"This cancels one identified equity order in the specified eligible account.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"cancel_equity_order","category":"order.cancel","arguments":{"account_number":"{account_id}","order_id":"{order_id}"},"result":{"accepted":"data.accepted"},"reason":"This cancels one identified equity order in the specified eligible account.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"cancel_option_exercise":{"contract":{"name":"cancel_option_exercise","title":null,"description":"Cancel all queued exercise requests for an option position. Pass the same account_number and option_id used for exercise_option. Internally looks up all queued exercise events for that option and cancels each one. Typically there is one; multiple means the user submitted separate exercise batches. Only cancels events in state=queued — events already processing are rejected by the broker. Always confirm with the user before calling.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Brokerage account that owns the exercise. Must be agentic_allowed=true."},"option_id":{"type":"string","description":"Option instrument UUID — the same option_id used for exercise_option. The tool looks up the queued exercise for this option and cancels it."}},"required":["account_number","option_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"cancelled_count":{"type":"integer","description":"Number of exercise requests successfully cancelled."},"events":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Exercise event UUID."},"state":{"type":"string","description":"queued (submitted, not yet processed — cancellable via cancel_option_exercise) | confirmed (processing complete, irrevocable) | voided (cancelled) | canceled (cancelled by customer via the cancel endpoint) | reversed (reversed by broker)."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"exercise (normal) | generic (index options in pending state — index options cannot be manually exercised)."},"quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Contracts exercised."},"option_id":{"type":"string","description":"Option instrument UUID."},"chain_id":{"type":"string","description":"Option chain UUID."},"account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Brokerage account number. Mask all but the last 4 digits when displaying to the user."},"direction":{"type":"string","description":"debit = call exercise (cash paid to acquire shares) | credit = put exercise (cash received for delivering shares)."},"total_cash_amount":{"type":"string","description":"Absolute cash amount of the exercise: strike × multiplier × contracts for calls; net proceeds for puts."},"event_date":{"type":"string","description":"Settlement date of the exercise (YYYY-MM-DD)."},"ref_id":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Idempotency key echoed from the request."},"underlying_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Underlying spot price at exercise time. Nil when not yet available."},"created_at":{"type":"string","description":"ISO 8601 timestamp when the exercise request was created."},"updated_at":{"type":"string","description":"ISO 8601 last update time."}},"required":["id","state","type","quantity","option_id","chain_id","account_number","direction","total_cash_amount","event_date","created_at"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Cancelled exercise events, one per exercise batch that was queued. Typically one entry; multiple means separate exercise submissions were made for this option."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["cancelled_count","events"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"cancelled_count tells the user how many exercise requests were cancelled. For each event in events[], surface state (voided = cancelled) and quantity so the user knows which batches were stopped. If cancelled_count=0, there was nothing to cancel — the exercise may have already been processed. On partial failure (some cancelled, some rejected), the successfully cancelled ones are in events[]; report the error for the ones that failed."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:cde4cb61cd21543769771334012de8c734f7dd6db7f53da6766b128fe1902d16","contract_hash":"sha256:7244d444a70a88fd80a734ed4dfddc208ea158b3c6e157d4333fe8d61a19c8e2"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"cancel_option_exercise","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"cancel_option_order":{"contract":{"name":"cancel_option_order","title":null,"description":"Cancel an open option order by account_number + order_id. Always confirm with the user before calling. Resolve order_id via get_option_orders if the user refers to it by description; pass the same account_number you used there. Requires an agentic_allowed=true account; non-agentic accounts are rejected. Cancellation may be rejected if the order has already filled, was already cancelled, or is otherwise ineligible.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Brokerage account that owns the order. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts. Must be agentic_allowed=true. Mismatches against the order's owning account are rejected."},"order_id":{"type":"string","description":"Order UUID from get_option_orders. Must live in account_number."}},"required":["account_number","order_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"accepted":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the broker accepted the cancel request."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["accepted"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"accepted=true means the broker accepted the cancel request, NOT that the order is already cancelled (cancellation is asynchronous). For the final state, call get_option_orders: state 'pending_cancelled' = in flight; 'cancelled' = succeeded; any filled state = a fill raced the cancel. Offer to check the final state. On error, the cancel was rejected outright — report verbatim."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:a407058f3e9b726da0609b852c729ed2b1adb9c72a31ed11c548ff45bd110350","contract_hash":"sha256:c8fcf83ac3f2465a918916fa4c5ad2d4bb345454c3486f64464e02ce6ac62b99"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"cancel_option_order","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"create_scan":{"contract":{"name":"create_scan","title":null,"description":"Create a new saved scanner (screener) on the user's account — or, with scan_id, update an existing one by appending a new configuration version. Filters can be enum-based (from get_scanner_filter_specs) or expression-based (a raw market-data expression built from get_scanner_datapoints). Returns the scan's id, title, applied filters, and live market results.

Prefer an enum filter_type whenever one covers the request: enum filters are pre-validated and render as standard, user-editable filters in Legend. Build a raw expression only when no enum filter covers the request, and validate it with preview_scan before saving it here. This is the only tool that saves expression filters — update_scan_filters rejects them — so to change a scan that has an expression filter, call this tool with that scan's scan_id and the full desired filter set.

Columns display values, filters screen. To show a datapoint in results without restricting matches, pass it in columns — never fake it with a no-op filter like ">= 0", which pollutes the scan's filter list. A column is a display_name plus an expression, or a standard column's display name alone. A couple of contextual columns supporting the filters make a scan read better in Legend.

Two execution paths:
- New scan, enum-only filters (or none), no columns: composes multiple Beacon operations — create the scan, apply the preset configuration if non-INITIAL, apply filters, set the title. If a step after the initial create fails, the scan still exists in its partial state; the response surfaces what was applied, and update_scan_filters / update_scan_config can fix the rest.
- scan_id set, any expression filter present, or any columns present: a single transactional Beacon call that persists the filters and columns as a new ACTIVE configuration version (on the given scan, or on a brand-new one). All-or-nothing — an expression the market-data provider rejects means NOTHING is persisted, and the provider's validation error is returned. Earlier versions of a scan are never edited. A non-INITIAL preset cannot be combined with this path.

Parameters:
- scan_id (optional) — update this existing scan instead of creating one. REPLACE semantics: the new version holds exactly the filters and columns passed, so read the current set via get_scans first and send the complete intended set. Cortex-managed scans are rejected.
- preset (optional) — starting preset for a new scan. Default: DAILY_GAINERS when no filters supplied, INITIAL when filters supplied. Valid values: INITIAL, DAILY_GAINERS, DAILY_LOSERS, HIGH_OPTIONS_VOLUME_IV, UPCOMING_EARNINGS.
- filters (optional for a new scan, required with scan_id) — array of filter specs, enum and/or expression. Call get_scanner_filter_specs for enum filters; call get_scanner_datapoints before composing an expression.
- columns (optional) — extra result columns on top of the filters' own columns and the standard defaults. An expression matching a standard column's canonical form is saved as that standard column, canonical name included (e.g. "optionsPutDayVolume" always saves as "Total put volume").
- title (optional) — custom human-readable name for the scan.

Example: to make "stocks with RSI > 70 and volume > 1M", call with
  preset = "INITIAL"
  filters = [
    {"filter_type": "FILTER_TYPE_RSI", "predicate": ">", "values": ["70"], "interval": "1d", "length": 14},
    {"filter_type": "FILTER_TYPE_VOLUME", "predicate": ">", "values": ["1000000"], "interval": "1d"}
  ]
  title = "High RSI + High Volume"

Example: to save "stocks where put option volume exceeds call option volume" (no enum filter compares two datapoints), showing both volumes and the ratio as context, call with
  filters = [
    {"expression": "optionsPutDayVolume > optionsCallDayVolume", "predicate": "=", "values": ["True"], "display_title": "Put exceeds call"}
  ]
  columns = [
    {"display_name": "Put volume", "expression": "optionsPutDayVolume"},
    {"display_name": "Call volume", "expression": "optionsCallDayVolume"},
    {"display_name": "Put/Call ratio", "expression": "optionsPutDayVolume / optionsCallDayVolume"}
  ]
  title = "Put hedging screen"
  (the first two save under their canonical standard names, "Total put volume" and "Total call volume")

Example: to tighten that saved screen later without creating a second scan, call with
  scan_id = "<its scan_id from get_scans>"
  filters = [the scan's current filters, copied from get_scans (expressions verbatim, enum filters by filter_type_enum), with the desired change applied]
  columns = [the scan's current extra columns, copied from get_scans, if they should be kept]","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"Optional. Update an existing scan by appending the given filters (and columns) as a NEW configuration version, which becomes the active one — earlier versions are preserved, never edited. The version holds exactly what is passed (REPLACE semantics, not merge): read the scan's current filters and columns with get_scans first and pass the complete intended set. This is how to change a scan that has expression filters, which update_scan_filters cannot carry. Cortex-managed scans are rejected. Omit to create a new scan."},"preset":{"type":"string","description":"Starting preset for the new scan. One of: INITIAL (no preset; only valid if filters are provided), DAILY_GAINERS, DAILY_LOSERS, HIGH_OPTIONS_VOLUME_IV, UPCOMING_EARNINGS. Defaults to DAILY_GAINERS when no filters are provided, INITIAL when filters are provided. A non-INITIAL preset cannot be combined with expression filters, columns, or scan_id."},"filters":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Wire-format enum name, e.g. "FILTER_TYPE_RSI". See the scanner-filter-specs resource for valid values. Omit when supplying expression."},"predicate":{"type":"string","description":"Wire-format enum name, e.g. "PREDICATE_GREATER_THAN". See the scanner-filter-specs resource for the predicates supported by each filter."},"values":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Threshold values. Single-element for unary predicates, two-element for BETWEEN, multi-element for IN_LIST/ANY_OF. For a boolean expression screen, exactly ["True"]."},"interval":{"type":"string","description":"Time granularity for time-series filters (e.g. "1d"). Use one of the supported_intervals from the filter's scanner-filter-specs entry. Not used with expression — encode granularity inside the expression."},"length":{"type":"integer","description":"Lookback length for filters that need one (e.g. RSI period of 14). Use one of the supported_lengths from the filter's scanner-filter-specs entry. Not used with expression.","minimum":-2147483648,"maximum":2147483647},"plot":{"type":"string","description":"Plot / price-field input for filters that have one (e.g. "open" or "close" for % Change). Use one of the supported_plots from the filter's scanner-filter-specs entry. Not used with expression."},"expression":{"type":"string","description":"Raw market-data expression to screen on, e.g. "dayVolume / volumeAvg(candleCount=30, candlePeriod=\"1d\", session=\"all\")" with a numeric predicate, or a whole comparison like "tradeAllDay.price > closeAvg(candleCount=50, candlePeriod=\"1d\", session=\"all\")" with predicate "=" and values ["True"]. Accepted by preview_scan (validate without saving) and create_scan (save); update_scan_filters rejects expressions — to change an expression filter on a saved scan, call create_scan with that scan's scan_id and the full filter set (a new configuration version is appended; earlier versions are preserved). Omit filter_type when set. Prefer an enum filter_type whenever one covers the request."},"display_title":{"type":"string","description":"Optional short label for an expression filter, shown as the results-column header (e.g. "Relative volume (30D)"). Only used with expression."}},"required":["predicate","values"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Custom filters, enum-based and/or expression-based. Enum filter: filter_type (FILTER_TYPE_... enum from get_scanner_filter_specs) plus predicate/values and optional interval/length/plot. Expression filter: expression (built from get_scanner_datapoints; omit filter_type) plus predicate/values and an optional display_title. Required when scan_id is set. Prefer an enum filter_type whenever one covers the request; validate an expression with preview_scan before saving it here."},"columns":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Column header, and the column's identity: matching an existing column's name (case-insensitively) customizes that column instead of adding a duplicate, and two columns cannot share a name. A filter with non-default interval/length names its column with those parameters (e.g. a 5-minute RSI filter's column is "RSI (14, 5M)") — matching it requires that exact name; a bare "RSI" next to it adds a separate, default-parameters RSI column. Without expression, must name a standard column (e.g. "Market cap", "RSI", "Volume") — an unknown name is rejected with the full list of valid ones."},"expression":{"type":"string","description":"Raw market-data expression computing the column's value, built from get_scanner_datapoints (same language as expression filters), e.g. "optionsPutDayVolume / optionsCallDayVolume". Omit to reference a standard column by display_name alone. If the expression equals a standard column's canonical form, the column is saved as that standard column and display_name is REPLACED by its canonical name (e.g. "optionsPutDayVolume" always saves as "Total put volume")."},"visible":{"type":["null","boolean"],"description":"Whether the column shows in results. When omitted, a NEW column is visible, but a column customizing an existing filter-created column keeps that column's current visibility (some filter columns are deliberately hidden) — pass an explicit value to change it. A hidden column is still computed and saved."},"order":{"type":["null","integer"],"description":"Relative ordering among the columns passed in this call: lower comes first, columns without an order go last in the order given. The scan's standard default columns (Symbol, Name, price, Volume, ...) always come before these.","minimum":-2147483648,"maximum":2147483647}},"required":["display_name"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Optional result columns to display on top of what the filters and the standard default columns already show. Each column: display_name plus either an expression (from get_scanner_datapoints) or nothing (a standard column referenced by name, e.g. "Market cap"). Columns display values, filters screen — to show a datapoint without restricting results, add a column here, never a no-op filter (e.g. >= 0). A couple of contextual columns supporting the filters make the scan read better in Legend."},"title":{"type":"string","description":"Optional custom title for the saved scan. If omitted: a new scan gets Beacon's default title for the preset, and a scan_id update keeps the scan's existing title."}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"result":{"type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"Scan identifier. Stable across reads and writes."},"scan_title":{"type":"string","description":"Human-readable name of the scan."},"total_items":{"type":"integer","description":"Total instruments matching the scan's filters. May exceed len(results) when the scan's frontend_limit is hit.","minimum":-2147483648,"maximum":2147483647},"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"ticker":{"type":"string","description":"Trading symbol (e.g. AAPL). Sourced from the scan's symbol column; empty when the scan has no symbol column visible."},"instrument_id":{"type":"string","description":"Robinhood instrument UUID. Pass to other trading tools that take an instrument_id."},"instrument_type":{"type":"string","description":"Robinhood's own asset classification: EQUITY, OPTION, INDEX, CRYPTO, FUTURES_PRODUCT, FUTURES_CONTRACT, COMBO. NOT the vocabulary the asset-type filter accepts, and not translatable to it: EQUITY covers both stocks and ETFs, which that filter distinguishes. To screen on asset type, use the values listed in the asset-type filter's options from get_scanner_filter_specs, never a value copied from this field."},"columns":{"type":"object","description":"Column display name -> cell value, for every visible column in the scan's configuration. Values are raw numeric strings, not display-formatted: columns whose header contains % hold ratios (multiply by 100 before presenting), large numbers can arrive in scientific notation, and floats carry precision noise. Always format before presenting. An empty string means the datapoint is undefined for that instrument; the row still matched the filters.","additionalProperties":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["ticker","instrument_id","instrument_type","columns"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Matched instruments, in the scan's current sort order. Live at time of execution."},"sorted_by":{"type":"string","description":"Current sort column + direction in human form (e.g. "Volume desc"). Empty when no sort is configured."},"filters_applied":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Display label of the column this filter screens on, as shown in Legend (e.g. "RSI", "Market cap"). This is a user-editable label, so it is for describing the filter to the user — do NOT send it back as filter_type when re-applying filters; use filter_type_enum for that."},"filter_type_enum":{"type":"string","description":"Wire-format enum name for this filter (e.g. "FILTER_TYPE_RSI") — the value to pass as a filter's filter_type when re-sending this filter to create_scan or update_scan_filters. FILTER_TYPE_CUSTOM is the exception: such a filter is defined by its expression, so re-create it by sending the expression field to create_scan and omitting filter_type. Never send FILTER_TYPE_CUSTOM as a filter_type — it would create an empty filter. Empty only when the filter has no recognized type."},"predicate":{"type":"string","description":"Comparison operator in symbolic form (e.g. ">", "<", "BETWEEN")."},"values":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Threshold values for the predicate. Single-element for >/</=, two-element for BETWEEN, multi-element for IN_LIST/ANY_OF."},"interval":{"type":"string","description":"Time granularity for time-series filters (e.g. "1d", "1h"). Empty for snapshot filters."},"length":{"type":"integer","description":"Lookback length for filters that need one (e.g. RSI period of 14). Zero/omitted for filters that don't take a length.","minimum":-2147483648,"maximum":2147483647},"plot":{"type":"string","description":"Plot / price-field input for filters that have one (e.g. % Change uses "open" or "close" to choose changeFromOpen vs changeFromClose). Empty for filters that don't take a plot."},"expression":{"type":"string","description":"Upstream market-data expression this filter screens on. Populated for every filter, standard or custom — an enum filter type is a preset that compiles to an expression upstream. Useful for explaining precisely what the filter measures (which interval, lookback and session it uses). When re-applying a standard filter, send filter_type_enum rather than this; for a FILTER_TYPE_CUSTOM filter this expression is exactly what to send, as the expression field of a create_scan filter."}},"required":["filter_type","predicate","values"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Filters in effect when the scan was run. Always populated on create_scan / update_scan_filters responses; optional on run_scan."},"cortex_managed":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when this scan was created or modified by Cortex. Read-only via MCP tools."}},"description":"The newly-created scan plus its initial live results.","required":["scan_id","scan_title","total_items","results","cortex_managed"],"additionalProperties":false}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["result"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"How to interpret the response:
- result.scan_id — the created scan (or, when scan_id was passed, that same scan: the update landed as a new configuration version on it). Pass this to run_scan, update_scan_filters, or update_scan_config in follow-up calls.
- result.scan_title — final title (custom if provided; else Beacon's default for a new scan, or the existing title on a scan_id update).
- result.filters_applied — the filter set actually in effect after the call. If this doesn't match what the user asked for, one of the composite steps failed silently — surface that to the user.
- result.results — initial live results (real-time market data at scan creation time).
- result.total_items — total matches. May exceed len(results) if the scan's frontend_limit is hit.

When presenting:
- Confirm the scan was created and note its title + filters_applied (so the user knows what was actually saved).
- Render the initial results as a table.
- Tell the user the scan is saved and can be re-run anytime with run_scan + the returned scan_id.
- If results is empty: tell the user no instruments match the filters right now, and suggest broadening them with update_scan_filters.

Error handling:
- "unknown preset X" → preset enum not recognized. List the valid presets to the user.
- "filter[N]: ..." → filter validation failure at index N. Tell the user which filter and why. Rejected before any Beacon call — nothing was created.
- "created by Cortex and cannot be modified" (with scan_id) → the target scan is Cortex-managed. Offer to create a fresh scan (omit scan_id) instead.
- Partial-failure responses (e.g. "scan X created but preset Y could not be applied") indicate a partial success on the enum path: the scan exists but is missing some of the intended state. Use filters_applied on the response to see what actually landed; mention this clearly to the user so they know whether they need to follow up with update_scan_filters.
- With expression filters there are no partial failures: an upstream validation error (e.g. "unresolved reference: X", "unsupported candle-period") means nothing was saved. Fix the expression — get_scanner_datapoints has the valid names and signatures — and call again, or iterate with preview_scan first."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:5c3b7e9835fa92635ab9d2280830ac494503669688e93e710732a56586d60879","contract_hash":"sha256:1d98822c23b42ea4780a1d7de2bf677a00394289da1eb11fd815eef6eaf2a356"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Scans are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"create_scan","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Scans are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"create_watchlist":{"contract":{"name":"create_watchlist","title":null,"description":"Create a new custom watchlist for the user. Confirm the name with the user before calling — this is a real write. Do not use this to follow a Robinhood-curated list (use follow_watchlist).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Name for the new watchlist (e.g. 'Tech Stocks'). Must be unique among the user's watchlists."},"icon_emoji":{"type":"string","description":"Emoji shown next to the name (one character)."},"display_description":{"type":"string","description":"Short description shown under the name."}},"required":["display_name"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"watchlist":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"List UUID. Pass to other watchlist tools (get_watchlist_items, add/remove_from_watchlist, update_watchlist) as list_id."},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Human-readable list name."},"display_description":{"type":"string","description":"Optional short description shown under the name."},"icon_emoji":{"type":"string","description":"Emoji shown alongside the name. Present on custom lists; absent on Robinhood-curated lists."},"owner_type":{"type":"string","description":"'custom' means a user-created list. 'robinhood' means a curated list the user is following. Use this to distinguish user-owned lists (writable: rename, delete items, add items) from curated lists (read + follow/unfollow only)."},"item_count":{"type":"integer","description":"Number of items in the list."},"allowed_object_types":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Which kinds of objects can be added to this list. Common values: instrument (US stock/ETF), currency_pair (crypto), index (market index), option_strategy (options watchlist — see add_option_to_watchlist), futures. add_to_watchlist supports instrument, currency_pair, and index; options use the dedicated add_option_to_watchlist tool; futures still require the Robinhood app."}},"description":"The newly created or updated watchlist.","required":["id","display_name","owner_type","item_count"],"additionalProperties":false}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["watchlist"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"On success the response includes the new list_id — pass it to add_to_watchlist to populate the list. If a 400 mentions 'unique set' the user already has a list with that name; suggest a different name."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:e54c594dfb0d995404068cedf5d409ee27ace7b5d319deca538464eb53ca6493","contract_hash":"sha256:e7732e7c18c36b5ffb64eb84b4fda160825bb793925374651b15cb846689415f"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Watchlists are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"create_watchlist","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Watchlists are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"exercise_option":{"contract":{"name":"exercise_option","title":null,"description":"Exercise a long options position — a call exercises the right to buy the underlying shares at the strike price; a put exercises the right to sell. Exercise is irrevocable once state moves past queued.

Never call this tool without asking the user to explicitly confirm the specific exercise first: state the option, quantity, and expected cash impact (debit for calls, credit for puts), then wait for their affirmative reply before calling. The user's original request to exercise is NOT itself sufficient confirmation — a generic "exercise my calls" does not confirm a specific option and quantity.

Position requirements: confirm via get_option_positions that the position type=long and quantity > 0.

Account requirements: confirm via get_accounts that the chosen account is agentic_allowed=true AND has option_level_2 or option_level_3. If agentic_allowed=false do NOT call. If option_level is empty or option_level_0, do NOT call; follow the get_accounts guide for how to direct the user to enroll.

Index options cannot be manually exercised and will be rejected. Exercises submitted during market hours execute the same day; requests submitted after market close — including on late-close trading days — are queued for overnight processing.

Parameter rules:
- quantity must be a positive integer and cannot exceed the position's available contracts.
- allow_shorts=true only applies to PUT exercises where the account does not own enough shares to deliver. Require explicit user confirmation before setting this — it creates a short equity position in the underlying stock.
- reason is optional but recommended; collect it from the user when they volunteer a motivation.
- ref_id: use the same UUID on retries of the same logical exercise; use a new UUID for a new exercise.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Brokerage account number. Must be agentic_allowed=true with option_level_2 or option_level_3."},"option_id":{"type":"string","description":"Option instrument UUID from get_option_positions or get_option_instruments. The position must be type=long."},"quantity":{"type":"integer","description":"Number of contracts to exercise (positive integer, minimum 1)."},"ref_id":{"type":"string","description":"Idempotency key (UUID). Generate once per logical exercise and re-send on retry. Omitting falls back to a server-generated key."},"reason":{"type":"string","description":"Optional exercise reason: covering_early_assignment | buying_stocks | not_enough_liquidity_or_spread_too_wide | hedging_position."},"allow_shorts":{"type":"boolean","description":"When true, allows a PUT exercise to proceed even when the account does not own enough shares to deliver — creating a short equity position. Requires explicit user confirmation that they intend to short the underlying stock. Default false."}},"required":["account_number","option_id","quantity"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"event":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Exercise event UUID."},"state":{"type":"string","description":"queued (submitted, not yet processed — cancellable via cancel_option_exercise) | confirmed (processing complete, irrevocable) | voided (cancelled) | canceled (cancelled by customer via the cancel endpoint) | reversed (reversed by broker)."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"exercise (normal) | generic (index options in pending state — index options cannot be manually exercised)."},"quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Contracts exercised."},"option_id":{"type":"string","description":"Option instrument UUID."},"chain_id":{"type":"string","description":"Option chain UUID."},"account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Brokerage account number. Mask all but the last 4 digits when displaying to the user."},"direction":{"type":"string","description":"debit = call exercise (cash paid to acquire shares) | credit = put exercise (cash received for delivering shares)."},"total_cash_amount":{"type":"string","description":"Absolute cash amount of the exercise: strike × multiplier × contracts for calls; net proceeds for puts."},"event_date":{"type":"string","description":"Settlement date of the exercise (YYYY-MM-DD)."},"ref_id":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Idempotency key echoed from the request."},"underlying_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Underlying spot price at exercise time. Nil when not yet available."},"created_at":{"type":"string","description":"ISO 8601 timestamp when the exercise request was created."},"updated_at":{"type":"string","description":"ISO 8601 last update time."}},"description":"The submitted exercise event.","required":["id","state","type","quantity","option_id","chain_id","account_number","direction","total_cash_amount","event_date","created_at"],"additionalProperties":false}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["event"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Surface event.state, direction, and total_cash_amount to the user. For calls: direction=debit (account pays cash to acquire shares at the strike price); for puts: direction=credit (account delivers shares and receives cash). If state=queued, tell the user the exercise is submitted and pending overnight processing, and that they can cancel it using cancel_option_exercise with the same option_id while it remains queued. On specific errors: incurs_large_loss means the option has meaningful remaining time value — the user is forgoing that premium by exercising early; present this clearly. not_enough_buying_power context carries buying_power and exercise_cost — show both. not_enough_shares context carries shares_owned and shares_to_exercise — show both."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:25762adc3aa9918387345224a0b8df05cabbff1699f98058fc2be98ac3831d67","contract_hash":"sha256:ca2bd721d4503c636598931e044cbb9cfcec79bc0579fb8c46996a0b2dcc35ab"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"exercise_option","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"follow_watchlist":{"contract":{"name":"follow_watchlist","title":null,"description":"Follow a Robinhood-curated list so it appears in the user's watchlists. Confirm with the user before calling. Use only for curated lists; the user already owns their custom lists.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"list_id":{"type":"string","description":"UUID of the Robinhood-curated list to follow. Obtain from get_popular_watchlists."}},"required":["list_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"follower":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"list_id":{"type":"string","description":"UUID of the list that was followed."},"user_id":{"type":"string","description":"UUID of the user that followed the list (always the caller)."},"owner_type":{"type":"string","description":"Always 'robinhood' for follow_watchlist — only Robinhood-curated lists are followable."},"created_at":{"type":"string","description":"ISO 8601 timestamp when the user first followed this list. The follower endpoint is idempotent — re-following an already-followed list returns the existing record, so this timestamp may be older than 'just now'."}},"description":"The new or pre-existing follower record. Omitted for unfollow which has no response body.","required":["list_id","user_id","owner_type","created_at"],"additionalProperties":false},"list_id":{"type":"string","description":"The list this call targeted."},"action":{"type":"string","description":"'followed' or 'unfollowed'."},"status":{"type":"string","description":"'ok' when the upstream accepted the operation."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["list_id","action","status"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"400 with 'you cannot follow a list you own' means the user already owns this list (no action needed). 400 with a follow-limit message means the user is at their max followed lists — they need to unfollow one first."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:5babbf34f2e6c82a3518dd8d948600420615510b1a8cd1e4197ec633bea53b85","contract_hash":"sha256:66e573b0d9c316680bbcfbb373ea032f49e6ee8baed46a3f21005a09475299ea"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Watchlists are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"follow_watchlist","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Watchlists are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_accounts":{"contract":{"name":"get_accounts","title":null,"description":"List the user's brokerage accounts. Each account includes an agentic_allowed field indicating whether it's tradable by you — accounts where it's false are read-only to you. Use this to look up account_number values needed by other tools. Exactly one account is tradable by you; when the user is choosing an account for a trade, use that account directly without asking. Does NOT return reliable buying power — route buying-power questions through get_portfolio.","input_schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"accounts":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Brokerage account number; pass to any tool that requires account_number. Mask all but the last 4 digits (e.g. '••••1234') when displaying to the user."},"rhs_account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Numeric brokerage account number — pass this (not account_number) to any nummus-backed tool that asks for an account identifier."},"rhc_account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Crypto account number for this account (e.g. 'RHC1234567'). Absent when no linked crypto account exists. Mask all but the last 4 digits (e.g. '••••1234') when displaying to the user."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"'cash', 'margin', or 'limited_margin' — the trading-permissions classification for the brokerage account. 'limited_margin' (instant settlement without full margin leverage) applies to accounts where full margin is unavailable, such as retirement (IRA), managed, and agentic accounts. Crypto accounts are never marginable, so a linked crypto account has no equivalent."},"unsettled_funds":{"type":"string","description":"Proceeds from recent sales not yet settled (cash accounts settle T+1), in the account's currency. Informational only and may lag live trading — this is NOT a spendable or order-gating figure; buying_power from get_portfolio is authoritative for what can be traded now. A cash-type account with unsettled_funds greater than 0 could trade with those proceeds immediately by upgrading to limited margin. Absent when upstream does not report it — treat as unknown, not zero."},"brokerage_account_type":{"type":"string","description":"Account type, e.g. 'individual', 'ira_traditional', 'ira_roth', 'ira_traditional_inherited', 'ira_roth_inherited', 'isa_stocks_and_shares'."},"nickname":{"type":"string","description":"User-set nickname; present alongside account_number when set. Cosmetic only — not an agentic_allowed or agentic-account signal."},"is_default":{"type":"boolean","description":"True for the user's default account. Surface when choosing among multiple accounts."},"agentic_allowed":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when this account is accessible to this agent specifically. An account with false may be agentic-enabled but scoped to a different agent type — do not tell the user it is disabled. Sole source of truth for eligibility — never infer it from nickname text. review_*/place_*/cancel_* tools reject accounts where this is false."},"option_level":{"type":"string","description":"Options approval: 'option_level_2' (long calls/puts, covered calls, cash-secured puts), 'option_level_3' (spreads and complex strategies), or empty/'option_level_0' (not approved)."},"management_type":{"type":"string","description":"Management classification (e.g. 'managed') when applicable; layered on top of brokerage_account_type rather than replacing it."},"affiliate":{"type":"string","description":"Affiliate / region code (e.g. 'RHF', 'RHUK', 'RHSG'). Affects feature availability for the account."},"state":{"type":"string","description":"Account state — 'active' is normal; anything else (deactivated, restricted, etc.) means the account cannot trade normally."},"deactivated":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the account is currently deactivated."},"permanently_deactivated":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the account is permanently closed (cannot be reactivated)."}},"required":["account_number","rhs_account_number","type","brokerage_account_type","is_default","agentic_allowed","option_level","state","deactivated","permanently_deactivated"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"The user's brokerage accounts. Empty when the user has none."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["accounts"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Sort the list deterministically when presenting: the default account first, agentic accounts (agentic_allowed=true) second, then other individual accounts, then retirement (IRA) accounts. Present account_number, rhc_account_number (label it "Crypto Account"), brokerage_account_type (label it "Account Type" — a linked crypto account always shares it, so never add a separate crypto account type column), type (label it "Brokerage Trading Type"), nickname (if set), and is_default — in that column order. In the Crypto Account column show "N/A" for accounts with an empty rhc_account_number; omit the column entirely only when no account has one. When referring to the account in user-facing prose (e.g. "your <X> account"), use nickname when set; fall back to brokerage_account_type otherwise. When displaying account_number or rhc_account_number to the user, mask all but the last 4 digits (e.g. '••••1234'); pass the full value to other tools unchanged — including get_option_level_upgrade_info and any fallback upgrade URL; masking breaks the link. Flag agentic_allowed when the user is choosing an account for a trade. There is exactly one agentic_allowed=true account — use it directly rather than asking which account to trade. agentic_allowed is caller-relative — true means accessible to this agent, false means this agent cannot act on it (the account may still be agentic-enabled for a different agent). Never state agentic_allowed's field name or raw boolean value to the user. Do not use nickname to determine agentic-account eligibility. Skip false accounts for trade operations; if the user asks why, say the account is not accessible to this agent, not that it needs to be enabled. When option_level is empty or 'option_level_0' and the user wants options, call get_option_level_upgrade_info with the account_number; if that tool is unavailable, direct the user to https://applink.robinhood.com/upgrade_options?account_number=<that account's account_number> (embed the full unmasked account_number in the URL). management_type='managed' is layered on brokerage_account_type — surface alongside, not as a replacement. For tools that ask for an account identifier on a crypto-backed flow (get_crypto_positions, future crypto write tools), pass rhs_account_number; for everything else (equities, options, etc.) pass account_number. Do not add an unsettled_funds column to the account table — surface it only via the following rule. Whenever you report an account's funds, value, or buying power and that account has type='cash' with unsettled_funds greater than 0, tell the user those unsettled proceeds could be traded immediately with a limited-margin upgrade, and — if the get_limited_margin_upgrade_info tool is available — call it with the account_number and share the appropriate upgrade link. If that tool is not available, say nothing about limited margin (there is no fallback). "}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:21afbfff7211747f1551362a6a8806f9e4b76e2d5537fefd71b97d0129342cb3","contract_hash":"sha256:55b99129976daab68eb463dbd56eacadea781fb14b3fac03afdb8111d0868e6f"},"category":"read.accounts","arguments":{},"result":{"items":"data.accounts","account":"account_number","eligible":"agentic_allowed","kind":"brokerage_account_type"},"reason":"This lists brokerage accounts and supplies the broker’s explicit eligibility signal and account type.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_accounts","category":"read.accounts","arguments":{},"result":{"items":"data.accounts","account":"account_number","eligible":"agentic_allowed","kind":"brokerage_account_type"},"reason":"This lists brokerage accounts and supplies the broker’s explicit eligibility signal and account type.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_crypto_account_onboarding_info":{"contract":{"name":"get_crypto_account_onboarding_info","title":null,"description":"Get the link a user opens to sign the crypto agreement and open a crypto account. Call when the user wants to trade crypto but has no crypto account.","input_schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"already_onboarded":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the user already has at least one crypto account — onboarding_url is empty and no signup is needed. False when they have none and should open the link to sign up."},"onboarding_url":{"type":"string","description":"Link for the user to sign the crypto agreement and open a crypto account. The user must log in to their Robinhood account at the link to sign. Present it as a tappable link; never call it programmatically. Empty when already_onboarded is true."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["already_onboarded"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"If already_onboarded is true, the user already has a crypto account, so no new signup is needed — do NOT present a link (the signup link cannot create or re-activate an account when one already exists). Tell them they already have a crypto account; do not claim it is active or ready to trade. If they say they still cannot trade crypto, their account may be deactivated, which is a separate reactivation flow this tool does not cover — direct them to Robinhood support rather than the link. Otherwise, send onboarding_url to the user as a tappable link, and tell them they must log in to their Robinhood account at the link to review and sign the crypto user agreement. After they sign, their crypto account(s) are provisioned — this tool does not create the account or sign on the user's behalf. Signing provisions crypto accounts for all of the user's eligible brokerage accounts, so a user who has an agentic brokerage account also gets an agentic crypto account. Once the user confirms they have finished, call get_accounts again with a fresh request to pick up the new crypto account before retrying; do not reuse a prior get_accounts result, as the account does not exist until the user completes this flow."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:59fe89d9d380ed77a1cd921508668b958809d9469cda1862a9a228267babfe90","contract_hash":"sha256:49ddaecb45fdf85b39a880bde8b8bdc1dc38f2ff795026e67b4ee3dc142c3149"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto account onboarding is outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_crypto_account_onboarding_info","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto account onboarding is outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_crypto_orders":{"contract":{"name":"get_crypto_orders","title":null,"description":"List crypto order history for an account — newest first. Open and closed orders, including fills, cancellations, and rejections. Pass order_id to retrieve a single order by UUID.

Filtering tips:
- Prefer narrow queries: combine state (or state_group), symbol, and/or created_at_gte for specific questions.
- created_at_gte: interpret relative times in the user's timezone, convert to UTC before sending.
- updated_at_gte: useful when polling for order fills or state transitions.
- symbol triggers a symbol→currency_pair_id lookup; omit it if you don't need it.

When the user asks for "orders" without specifying equity, options, or crypto, call get_equity_orders, get_option_orders, and get_crypto_orders in parallel.

For requests spanning all accounts, re-fetch the account list with get_accounts first — a list from earlier in the conversation may be missing newly created accounts.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"rhs_account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Numeric brokerage account number (the 'rhs_account_number' field on get_accounts entries — distinct from the alphanumeric 'account_number'). Required."},"order_id":{"type":"string","description":"Filter to a single order by UUID. The response shape is unchanged (results[] with at most one entry); empty when the order does not belong to the account."},"state":{"type":"string","description":"Filter by single state: queued, confirmed, partially_filled, filled, canceled, rejected, failed, voided. For open-vs-closed shortcuts, use state_group instead."},"state_group":{"type":"string","description":"Filter by state group: 'open' or 'closed'. Quick shortcut — 'open' covers queued/confirmed/partially_filled, 'closed' covers filled/canceled/rejected/failed/voided. Mutually exclusive with state."},"side":{"type":"string","description":"Filter by side: 'buy' or 'sell'."},"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Filter by crypto symbol (e.g. 'BTC', 'ETH', or 'BTC-USD'). Triggers a symbol→currency_pair_id lookup before the orders call."},"created_at_gte":{"type":"string","description":"Lower bound (inclusive) on created_at. ISO 8601 UTC; naive values are interpreted as UTC."},"updated_at_gte":{"type":"string","description":"Lower bound (inclusive) on updated_at. ISO 8601 UTC. Useful for polling for fills — each state transition bumps updated_at."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"Pagination cursor. Omit for the first page; for the next page, pass the cursor query param from the prior response's next URL."}},"required":["rhs_account_number"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"rhs_account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Echo of the brokerage account number this page was queried with. Every order in results belongs to this account — when querying multiple accounts in parallel, attribute orders using this echo, not memory of which call was which."},"crypto_account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Crypto account number (e.g. 'RHC1234567') these orders belong to. Present THIS as the account to the user — not the brokerage account number used to look it up. When absent, refer to the account as the user's linked crypto account."},"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Order UUID. Needed by cancel_crypto_order (M2.2)."},"ref_id":{"type":"string","description":"Client-supplied idempotency key from order placement. Useful for reconciling agent-placed orders against records the agent kept."},"account_id":{"type":"string","description":"Crypto account UUID this order belongs to. Matches the account_id on get_crypto_positions rows."},"currency_pair_id":{"type":"string","description":"Pair UUID (e.g. BTC-USD). Pass to get_crypto_quotes for current price, or match against get_currency_pairs.id."},"currency_code":{"type":"string","description":"Asset currency code (e.g. 'BTC', 'ETH'). Useful for grouping orders by coin without joining against get_currency_pairs."},"side":{"type":"string","description":"'buy' or 'sell'."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"'market', 'limit', 'stop_loss', or 'stop_limit'. 'stop_loss' is a stop-triggered market order — despite the name it applies to buy stops too; the equity/option tools call the same concept 'stop_market'. ALWAYS call these by their app names when speaking to the user, including when listing what types are supported: 'stop_loss' is a 'stop order' and 'stop_limit' a 'stop limit order'; the raw values are tool inputs only."},"state":{"type":"string","description":"Raw lifecycle state: new, queued, unconfirmed, confirmed, partially_filled, filled, canceled, rejected, failed, voided. Combine with derived_state for clearer end-state classification."},"derived_state":{"type":"string","description":"Normalized lifecycle classification, e.g. 'open' / 'closed' / similar shorthand the upstream computes from raw state + fills. Prefer over state for user-facing summaries."},"state_group":{"type":"string","description":"'open' or 'closed' — the headline answer to 'is this order still working?'."},"time_in_force":{"type":"string","description":"'gtc' (good till canceled), 'gfd' (good for day), 'ioc' (immediate or cancel), 'gfw' (good for week), 'gfm' (good for month)."},"quantity":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Originally-requested asset quantity. On dollar-based orders the server derives it at placement: from the quote for market and from the stop price for stop_loss (treat those as estimated until fills confirm them), and from the limit price for limit/stop_limit (exact at placement)."},"cumulative_quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Total asset quantity filled so far. Less than quantity while partially filled; equal once filled."},"canceled_quantity":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Quantity that was canceled before fill (only populated on partial-fill-then-cancel paths)."},"price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Order price (interpretation depends on type — limit price for limit; for stop_loss it is the collared worst-case execution bound, NOT the trigger, which lives in stop_price; for market it is the raw quote side-price on a preview_crypto_order response — the same price the app displays, NOT collared — but the collared worst-case execution bound on placed orders; stablecoin pairs are never collared, so their preview and placed prices both carry the raw quote). Use limit_price / stop_price for the unambiguous fields."},"limit_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Limit price for limit / stop_limit orders. Null for market / stop_loss."},"stop_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Stop trigger price for stop_loss / stop_limit orders. Null for market / limit."},"average_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Volume-weighted average fill price across executions. Null until the first fill."},"entered_price":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Price the user originally entered (pre-collaring). Different from limit_price after server-side collaring adjusts the order."},"rounded_executed_notional":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Total notional filled so far in the quote currency, rounded to 2 decimals."},"executions":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Execution UUID."},"price":{"type":"string","description":"Reported fill price per unit asset (e.g. USD per BTC). For the price the user actually paid after venue adjustments, use effective_price."},"effective_price":{"type":"string","description":"Per-unit price after venue fees or price adjustments are applied — closer to the user's realized fill economics than price."},"quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Asset quantity filled in this execution."},"notional":{"type":"string","description":"effective_price * quantity, rounded to 2 decimals where applicable."},"exchange_name":{"type":"string","description":"Routing venue name. Treat as informational; do not surface unless the user asks about routing."},"timestamp":{"type":"string","description":"When the fill occurred (UTC)."}},"required":["id","price","effective_price","quantity","notional","timestamp"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Per-fill detail. Reference for per-execution timing or price questions; for headline 'what did this fill at?' use average_price."},"initiator_type":{"type":"string","description":"Source that placed the order: 'api_trading', 'trading_view', 'recurring', 'paycheck', 'rh_assistant', 'agentic_trading' (when nummus adds that enum value), or one of the internal crypto-specific values. Tells the user whether they placed this order via app, API, recurring buy, or an agent."},"speculative":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the order was created as a speculative pre-trade check (no upstream side effect). Should always be false on real placed orders; populated read-only by upstream."},"created_at":{"type":"string","description":"When the order was created (UTC)."},"updated_at":{"type":"string","description":"Last server-side state update (UTC) — fill, cancel, reject, etc."},"canceled_at":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"When the cancel was acknowledged. Null when the order has not been canceled."},"routing":{"type":"string","description":"How the order is routed for execution. Present verbatim as the routing line item; absent when routing information is unavailable."},"rounded_estimated_notional_with_estimated_fee":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Estimated total cost (buy) or net proceeds (sell) in the quote currency, with ONLY the estimated fee already included. It does NOT include any additional taxes or deductions."},"rounded_uncollared_estimated_notional_with_estimated_fee":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Same as rounded_estimated_notional_with_estimated_fee but before price collaring. Null when collaring does not apply."},"rounded_executed_notional_with_fee":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Notional actually executed so far only including fees without netting additional taxes, in the quote currency. Grows as fills come in; 0 before the first fill. For the executed figure net of all taxes and fees use net_rounded_executed_notional."},"total_executed_notional":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Total executed notional so far only including fees without netting additional taxes. Null until there are fills."},"net_rounded_estimated_notional":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Estimated total cost (buy) or credit (sell) net of ALL taxes and fees. On a preview, present this as the estimated total cost or credit line item alongside the separate estimated_fee value. Never subtract the fee or taxes from it again. Null when an order has fills."},"net_rounded_executed_notional":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Executed total cost (buy) or credit (sell) net of ALL taxes and fees — the definitive amount actually debited or credited. Null before the first fill. Grows as fills come in. Never subtract the fee or any taxes from it again."},"fees":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"fee_structure":{"type":"string","description":"How the fee was computed (e.g. a fixed percentage or a volume-tiered rate)."},"fee_data":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"fee_type":{"type":"string","description":"Fee category (e.g. a transaction/spread fee)."},"fee_amount":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Fee amount in the quote currency (USD)."},"fee_ratio":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Rate this fee was computed at, when applicable."}},"description":"This fee's amount, type, and rate.","additionalProperties":false}},"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Itemized fee breakdown for exchange-routed orders. Empty or absent when the order carries no itemized fees."},"tax_withholding":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"withholding_rate":{"type":"string","description":"Withholding rate preformatted as a percent (e.g. '24%'), aggregated across the federal and any state portion. Print verbatim. Absent when no rate is available."},"estimated_withholding_amount":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Estimated USD to be withheld from this sell's proceeds. Present only while cumulative_quantity is 0. Exactly one of this and total_withholding_amount is ever present, so read the one that is there."},"total_withholding_amount":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Actual USD withheld from proceeds across fills so far (final once fully filled). Present only once cumulative_quantity is positive. Exactly one of this and estimated_withholding_amount is ever present, so read the one that is there."}},"description":"Backup withholding on this sell order's proceeds. Present only when withholding applies (sell orders for subject users; never on IRA accounts) — when absent, do not mention withholding. amount and withholding_rate are the display-ready figure and percent.","additionalProperties":false},"fee":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Fee for this order in the quote currency (USD on USD-quoted pairs) — an estimate before any fill; once filled, the amount collected on fills so far (final when fully filled). Absent when the order carries no itemized fees (typical of Market Maker Routing) — treat absence as no fee data, not a $0 charge."},"fee_rate":{"type":"string","description":"Rate this order's fee was computed at, preformatted: the bare percent on single-rate fee pricing (e.g. '0.95%'), suffixed with the liquidity outcome on maker/taker-priced accounts — e.g. '0.05% maker', '0.1% taker', or '0.07% blended' for orders filled partly maker and partly taker. Absent when no fee rate applies."}},"required":["id","account_id","currency_pair_id","side","type","state","time_in_force","quantity","cumulative_quantity","created_at","updated_at"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Crypto orders on this page, newest first. Empty when the cursor has no rows."},"next":{"type":"string","description":"Next-page URL. Empty when there are no more pages."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["rhs_account_number","results"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"For the headline answer to "is this order still working?", use state_group ('open' vs 'closed'); raw state has finer granularity if the user asks why. For the fill price the user cares about, use average_price (VWAP across fills). cumulative_quantity vs quantity tells "how much filled?"; canceled_quantity only appears on partial-fill-then-cancel paths. Asset symbol is currency_code; pair UUID is currency_pair_id. For current market, call get_crypto_quotes with the pair symbol (construct as currency_code + "-USD" for USD-quoted pairs, or look up via get_currency_pairs) — get_crypto_quotes takes the symbol, NOT currency_pair_id. initiator_type tells how the order was placed (app / API / recurring / agent) — surface it when the agent didn't place this order. Per-fill executions[] are omitted from list responses to keep the page sized for an agent's context window; pass order_id to retrieve a single order with executions populated. Present currency_code, side, type (ALWAYS translated to the app's name: stop_loss = "stop order", stop_limit = "stop limit order" — never show the raw stop_loss/stop_limit values to the user), state, quantity (or cumulative_quantity when partially filled), average_price once filled, backup withholding on a sell whenever tax_withholding is present, created_at, and id when cancellation may follow; suppress other fields unless asked. When presenting multiple orders, add a Fee column when any order on the page carries fee or fee_rate — the fee value verbatim (label it estimated when the order has no fills yet), with the fee_rate value appended verbatim in parentheses when present, e.g. '$1.23 (0.05% maker)' or '$1.23 (0.95%)' — fee_rate carries its own maker/taker/blended qualifier, never re-derive or re-label it; an order with fee_rate but no fee shows the bare rate; '-' for orders with neither; omit the column entirely when no order on the page has either. For a single order, state the fee and rate the same way when present. Backup withholding: show whichever of tax_withholding.estimated_withholding_amount / total_withholding_amount is present (exactly one ever is), labeled "Estimated backup withholding" for the estimate and "Backup withholding" for the total, with the tax_withholding.withholding_rate value appended verbatim in parentheses, e.g. '$23.88 (24%)'; on a partially filled order phrase the total as withheld so far — never as final, and never compute an estimate for the remainder. When presenting multiple orders, add a Withholding column only when at least one order on the page carries tax_withholding, with '-' for orders that do not; when none does, do not mention withholding at all. Answer total cost/credit questions from whichever net_* field the order carries, never from rounded_executed_notional / rounded_estimated_notional_with_estimated_fee / total_executed_notional — those are gross of taxes like backup withholding and will overstate a subject order. An order with no tax_withholding has no withholding — never raise the subject for it or show it as $0. Every order on this page belongs to the account echoed in rhs_account_number / crypto_account_number — when querying several accounts in parallel, attribute each order from its own response's echo, never from memory; identify the account to the user by crypto_account_number."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:57cd28bb3e522619e448462d45fa48d04983e02de4108aa428fdbd84a965a40a","contract_hash":"sha256:7bc9657a139d9b0ff9a37ff2f72e8c8ba90642a13cf3af54d6a8d11fbcf986d1"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto orders are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_crypto_orders","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto orders are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_crypto_positions":{"contract":{"name":"get_crypto_positions","title":null,"description":"List open crypto positions for a specific brokerage account. Returns asset, quantity, transferable amount, and cost-basis breakdown.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"rhs_account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Numeric brokerage account number (the 'rhs_account_number' field on get_accounts entries — distinct from the alphanumeric 'account_number'). Required."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"Pagination cursor. Omit for the first page; for the next page, pass the cursor query param from the prior response's next URL."}},"required":["rhs_account_number"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"account_id":{"type":"string","description":"Brokerage account UUID this position belongs to."},"currency":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"code":{"type":"string","description":"Currency ticker (e.g. 'BTC', 'ETH', 'USD')."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Full currency name (e.g. 'Bitcoin', 'Ethereum')."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"'cryptocurrency' for crypto assets, 'fiat' for cash currencies."}},"description":"Asset currency this position holds. Use currency.code as the asset symbol.","required":["code","name","type"],"additionalProperties":false},"currency_pair_id":{"type":"string","description":"UUID of the canonical pair quoted against USD (e.g. BTC-USD). Pass in the currency_pair_ids array to add_to_watchlist / remove_from_watchlist. For current price call get_crypto_quotes with the pair SYMBOL (construct as currency.code + "-USD"), not this UUID. Empty when no such pair exists for this asset (rare)."},"quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Total quantity held in asset units (e.g. BTC), net of pending withdrawal holds only. For the amount the user can actually sell right now, use 'quantity_transferable'."},"quantity_transferable":{"type":"string","description":"Quantity available to sell or transfer right now — net of open sell orders, pending withdrawals, quarantine, and any other holds. This is the correct field for 'how much can I sell?', including for crypto purchased on instant funds. Strictly ≤ 'quantity'."},"quantity_held_for_sell":{"type":"string","description":"Quantity locked by open outgoing sell orders."},"cost_bases":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"direct_quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Quantity attributable to direct buys (excludes transfers and rewards)."},"direct_cost_basis":{"type":"string","description":"Total cost basis for direct_quantity (units of the quote currency, typically USD)."},"intraday_quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Portion of direct_quantity acquired today."},"intraday_cost_basis":{"type":"string","description":"Total cost basis for intraday_quantity."}},"required":["direct_quantity","direct_cost_basis","intraday_quantity","intraday_cost_basis"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Direct-purchase cost basis. Tracks only the portion of the position that came from buys — quantity acquired via transfer, reward, or fork is not represented here, so sum(direct_quantity) can be less than the holding's quantity. Multiple entries appear after forks/splits (e.g. BCH/BSV)."}},"required":["account_id","currency","quantity","quantity_transferable","quantity_held_for_sell"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Open crypto positions on this page. Empty when the cursor has no rows."},"next":{"type":"string","description":"Next-page URL. Empty when there are no more pages."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Sellable quantity: use `quantity_transferable`, not `quantity` — `quantity_transferable` is the amount available to sell right now (already nets out open sell orders, pending withdrawals, holds, quarantine, and instant-funds restrictions); `quantity` only subtracts pending withdrawals. The two are equal in the common case but diverge when there are open sells or unsettled instant buys. Asset name comes from currency.code; for current price, call get_crypto_quotes with the pair symbol (construct as `currency.code + "-USD"` for USD-quoted pairs, or look up via get_currency_pairs) — note that get_crypto_quotes takes the symbol, NOT currency_pair_id. For per-unit average buy price, sum direct_cost_basis and sum direct_quantity across all cost_bases entries (multi-entry rows appear after forks like BCH/BSV) and divide — the average only covers direct purchases. When sum(direct_quantity) is materially less than quantity, the rest came from transfers, rewards, or forks with no captured cost basis; surface that the average buy price applies only to a subset of the units. The intraday_* fields isolate today's portion when the user asks about today specifically. Suppress cost_bases when not asked. No market price here — for current value or P&L, multiply the get_crypto_quotes result by quantity."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:110b43e15f8670b5cf0e2bc5d3a2ea9ed078e69167c161d2e11eacb4a2d96184","contract_hash":"sha256:ed606f828459f5a2ae2ba8625c0df76ba9a54d0452b529cf61bc05c20c24c561"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto positions are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_crypto_positions","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto positions are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_crypto_quotes":{"contract":{"name":"get_crypto_quotes","title":null,"description":"Get real-time bid/ask/mark prices plus the previous close for one or more crypto pair symbols (e.g. BTC-USD).","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"symbols":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"One or more crypto pair symbols (e.g. 'BTC-USD', 'ETH-USD'). Hyphenated and unhyphenated forms are both accepted on input; the response symbol field comes back unhyphenated."},"timezone":{"type":"string","description":"Optional IANA timezone name (e.g. 'America/New_York', 'America/Los_Angeles') that anchors the previous-close (open_price) day boundary to the user's local midnight and sets the timezone the response timestamps (bid_time, ask_time, updated_at) are rendered in. Pass ONLY when the user's timezone is known from context — do NOT guess it, infer it from language, or default it. When omitted, the previous close is anchored to midnight US Eastern and timestamps are rendered in US Eastern. Must be a valid IANA name — not an abbreviation ('PST'), a UTC offset ('-08:00'), or 'Local'."},"rhs_account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Optional numeric brokerage account number (the 'rhs_account_number' from get_accounts). When supplied, bid/ask/mark and the previous close are priced on this account's execution routing — the venues its orders actually fill at — and the applied routing is echoed in routing. When omitted, prices use the caller's own routing (it is set at the user level, so any of their crypto accounts yields the same routing). A caller with no crypto account, or an account that cannot be resolved, receives market-maker-routed pricing."}},"required":["symbols"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Crypto pair symbol returned by upstream in unhyphenated form (e.g. 'BTCUSD'). To cross-reference with get_currency_pairs.symbol (which is hyphenated, e.g. 'BTC-USD'), strip the hyphen from that field or insert one before the last 3 characters of this one."},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Currency-pair instrument UUID. Pass in the currency_pair_ids array to add_to_watchlist / remove_from_watchlist — no separate get_currency_pairs call needed just to get the UUID. Also matches get_currency_pairs.id and the currency_pair_id on get_crypto_positions rows."},"bid_price":{"type":"string","description":"Highest current buy-order price. Zero when the book is closed or unavailable — do NOT present zero as a price."},"bid_time":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Timestamp of bid_price, rendered in the request timezone (the get_crypto_quotes 'timezone' parameter; US Eastern when not supplied). Present when the upstream included side timestamps; otherwise absent."},"ask_price":{"type":"string","description":"Lowest current sell-order price. Zero when the book is closed or unavailable."},"ask_time":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Timestamp of ask_price, rendered in the request timezone (the get_crypto_quotes 'timezone' parameter; US Eastern when not supplied). Present when the upstream included side timestamps; otherwise absent."},"mark_price":{"type":"string","description":"Reference midpoint computed from bid and ask. Zero when both sides of the book are unavailable."},"open_price":{"type":"string","description":"Previous close — the reference midpoint (same bid/ask-mid basis as mark_price) at the midnight day boundary of the request timezone (the get_crypto_quotes 'timezone' parameter; US Eastern when not supplied). Crypto trades continuously, so this boundary price is the prior day's close. Resets daily; NOT a last-trade price."},"routing":{"type":"string","description":"Execution routing these prices are quoted on, matching the routing on get_crypto_orders rows. bid_price, ask_price, mark_price, and open_price are all priced on this routing. Absent when routing information is unavailable."},"updated_at":{"type":"string","description":"Time this snapshot was last refreshed, rendered in the request timezone (the get_crypto_quotes 'timezone' parameter; US Eastern when not supplied) — the same zone that anchors open_price. Use to judge freshness — when stale, phrase as 'as of <time>' rather than 'current'."}},"required":["symbol","id","bid_price","ask_price","mark_price","open_price","updated_at"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"One entry per requested symbol with live market data. Empty if no symbol resolved."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Current price: prefer mark_price when both sides of the book are populated; if mark_price is zero, fall back to the most recent of bid_time / ask_time and quote the side that updated last. Drop bid or ask when zero — the book is unavailable on that side. Use updated_at to judge freshness; if it is more than a few seconds stale, phrase as "as of <time>" rather than "current". open_price is the previous close — in continuous crypto the midnight boundary price is the prior day's close. That boundary is midnight in the request timezone (the 'timezone' parameter), or US Eastern when none is supplied; response timestamps carry that same timezone's offset, so quote "as of" times in it directly. For change vs the previous close, compute (mark_price - open_price) / open_price. The response symbol comes back unhyphenated (e.g. 'BTCUSD'); the canonical form from get_currency_pairs is hyphenated ('BTC-USD') — strip the hyphen to cross-reference. bid/ask/mark reflect the execution routing reported in routing: the supplied account's routing when rhs_account_number was given, otherwise the caller's user-level routing (market maker routing when the caller has no crypto account). This is informational; place_order routing is selected per account at order time."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:c157b25b7fb0376282d1d0ab60d23f961560bcb91b9c3ffb8908b27184f114a3","contract_hash":"sha256:a4bd194107135bdef11a0156a13e4d6a18c13b8950a92c1dad0849577b60287c"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto quotes are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_crypto_quotes","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto quotes are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_currency_pairs":{"contract":{"name":"get_currency_pairs","title":null,"description":"List Robinhood-supported crypto currency pairs (e.g. BTC-USD, ETH-USD), including any with an active trading halt. Catalog-only coins that Robinhood does not offer are excluded. Use this to discover symbols and per-pair order constraints before calling get_crypto_quotes or referencing positions.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"Pagination cursor. Omit for the first page; for the next page, pass the cursor query param from the prior response's next URL."},"limit":{"type":"integer","description":"Maximum number of pairs to return on this page (clamped to [1, 700]). Defaults to 25 to keep the response sized for an agent's context window; raise it when the user wants the full catalog and is OK with a larger response."}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Currency-pair UUID. Pass to get_crypto_quotes via the symbol field, or match against the currency_pair_id on get_crypto_positions rows."},"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Canonical hyphenated symbol (e.g. 'BTC-USD'). Note: get_crypto_quotes returns the unhyphenated form (e.g. 'BTCUSD') in its symbol field; strip the hyphen here to cross-reference."},"display_symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Display-only override for the symbol (rarely set). When empty, treat symbol as the display value."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Full pair name (e.g. 'Bitcoin')."},"asset_currency":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Currency UUID."},"code":{"type":"string","description":"Ticker (e.g. 'BTC', 'USD')."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Full currency name (e.g. 'Bitcoin', 'U.S. Dollar')."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"'cryptocurrency' or 'fiat'."}},"description":"The asset side of the pair (e.g. BTC in BTC-USD).","required":["id","code","name","type"],"additionalProperties":false},"quote_currency":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Currency UUID."},"code":{"type":"string","description":"Ticker (e.g. 'BTC', 'USD')."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Full currency name (e.g. 'Bitcoin', 'U.S. Dollar')."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"'cryptocurrency' or 'fiat'."}},"description":"The quote side of the pair (typically USD).","required":["id","code","name","type"],"additionalProperties":false},"tradability":{"type":"string","description":"Pair-level eligibility: 'tradable' (both sides open), 'buy_only', 'sell_only', 'untradable', or 'limited'. Resolved for the authenticated user across all their account types; per-account-type detail is in tradability_by_account_type."},"tradability_by_account_type":{"type":"object","description":"Per-account-type tradability override (key e.g. 'individual', 'ira_roth', value as in tradability). Empty when only the headline applies.","additionalProperties":{"type":"string"}},"display_only":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the pair is shown for discovery but cannot be ordered."},"min_order_size":{"type":"string","description":"Minimum order quantity in asset units (e.g. 0.00000001 BTC)."},"max_order_size":{"type":"string","description":"Maximum order quantity in asset units."},"min_order_quantity_increment":{"type":"string","description":"Quantity step size — order quantities must be a multiple of this value."},"min_order_price_increment":{"type":"string","description":"Limit-price step size — prices must be a multiple of this value."},"min_order_quote_amount":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Minimum order notional in the quote currency (USD). Null for unauthenticated callers or pairs without a notional floor."},"market_orders_only":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when only market orders are accepted on this pair (no limit / stop variants)."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Currency-pair type (typically 'cryptocurrency')."},"halted":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when this pair has an active halt in one or more regions right now. Convenience flag for halted_regions being non-empty. Derived from the /halts/summary/ endpoint at call time; distinct from tradability, which reflects standing eligibility rather than a live halt event."},"halted_regions":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Region codes where this pair currently has an active halt (e.g. ['NY','TX']). The sentinel 'ALL' denotes a global halt that applies to every region. Omitted when the pair is not halted. A region-scoped entry may be one-sided (e.g. sell-only) — do not assume the pair is fully suspended."}},"required":["id","symbol","name","asset_currency","quote_currency","tradability","display_only","min_order_size","max_order_size","min_order_quantity_increment","min_order_price_increment","market_orders_only","halted"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Robinhood-supported currency pairs on this page, including pairs with an active halt (halted=true). Catalog-only coins not offered by Robinhood are excluded. Empty when the cursor has no rows."},"next":{"type":"string","description":"Next-page URL. Empty when there are no more pages."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Render pairs as a markdown table with columns: Symbol | Name | Pair ID | Min Order | Max Order | Min Increment | Min Price Increment | Min Notional | Mkt Only | Restrictions | Halted. Formatting: Symbol → symbol; Name → asset_currency.name (e.g. 'Aave', not the full pair name); Pair ID → id truncated to the segment before the first '-'; Min Order → min_order_size; Max Order → max_order_size with comma separators; Min Increment → min_order_quantity_increment; Min Price Increment → '$' + min_order_price_increment; Min Notional → '$' + min_order_quote_amount, or '—' when null; Mkt Only → 'Yes'/'No' from market_orders_only; Restrictions → halted_regions joined by ', ' ('ALL' = a global halt), or 'None' when empty; Halted → 'True' when halted else '—'. When Halted is True the pair has a live halt in the listed regions — it may be one-sided (e.g. sell-only) and should not be assumed freely orderable. Only Robinhood-supported pairs are listed; catalog-only coins Robinhood does not offer are already excluded."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:6a7c8201e822ce3dafde83214e79b2139aea3105b5dc1c7de9bdbf468f8c12af","contract_hash":"sha256:faef448c64cde220b0580a27a0489732592525150b3d60e90815a6f3d2c1c117"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto instruments are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_currency_pairs","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Crypto instruments are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_earnings_calendar":{"contract":{"name":"get_earnings_calendar","title":null,"description":"List earnings reports scheduled across the market over a date window (up to 31 days), optionally limited to high-market-cap names. Returns one entry per report event — estimated/actual EPS, report date and timing (am/pm), and company-verification status. Use this for market-wide discovery ("what large-caps report this week?"). For a specific known ticker, use get_earnings_results instead. Read-only.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"start_date":{"type":"string","description":"Window anchor, YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to today (US/Eastern) when omitted."},"days":{"type":"integer","description":"Window length in days, measured from start_date. Defaults to 7. Positive = forward window (e.g. 7 = the next 7 days, inclusive of start_date); negative = look-back window (e.g. -7 = the 7 days ending at start_date). Must be a non-zero value between -31 and 31 — windows wider than 31 days are rejected."},"filter":{"type":"string","description":"Optional result filter. Set to 'high_market_cap' to limit the calendar to high-market-cap names (market cap over $1B) — useful for 'what large-caps report this week' style questions. Omit for all names."}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Ticker symbol the earnings event belongs to."},"year":{"type":"integer","description":"Fiscal year of the report (e.g. 2026)."},"quarter":{"type":"integer","description":"Fiscal quarter of the report (1-4)."},"eps":{"type":"object","properties":{"estimate":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Expected (estimated) EPS for the quarter. Null when no estimate is available for this quarter."},"actual":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Reported EPS for the quarter. Null for upcoming quarters (not yet reported) — pair with report.date to tell the two apart."}},"description":"Estimated and actual earnings per share for the quarter. Both sides may be null — see field docs.","required":["estimate","actual"],"additionalProperties":false},"report":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"date":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"YYYY-MM-DD report date. Present whenever the parent report block is non-null — use the parent's null/non-null state, not this field, to detect 'no scheduled event'."},"timing":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"'am' (before market) or 'pm' (after market). Null when timing is not yet known — only distinguishes before/after market, not an exact time."},"verified":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the company has confirmed the report date. False when the date is tentative (not yet company-confirmed)."}},"description":"Report scheduling — date, am/pm timing, company-verification flag. Null when upstream has no scheduled event for this quarter yet.","required":["date","timing","verified"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["symbol","year","quarter","eps","report"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Earnings report events in the window, one per company-quarter, sorted ascending by report date. Empty array when no reports fall in the window."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Each entry is one company's report event within the window, sorted ascending by report date. The window spans days from start_date (positive = forward, negative = look-back). Distinguish "upcoming" from "already reported" by eps.actual: null means not yet reported. When report.verified is false, present the date as tentative rather than confirmed. An empty results array means no reports fall in the window (with filter=high_market_cap, no high-market-cap names do) — not an error. This tool does NOT return an "expected move" — pair with options data for implied-volatility-based moves."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:f1d290a23129c9a6a0bce7f18302598f3a21f6e92fb344c35ec74aea0ed4d267","contract_hash":"sha256:5ae4bcdeaec2cd544c78f6e0f0418e1941c518d66c4b4122c33fbfd61088dec0"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Earnings and fundamentals are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_earnings_calendar","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Earnings and fundamentals are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_earnings_results":{"contract":{"name":"get_earnings_results","title":null,"description":"Get recent and upcoming earnings for ONE equity symbol — estimated/actual EPS, report date and timing (am/pm), and company-verification status. Returns the trailing up to 8 quarters. Use this for earnings-timing questions ("does AAPL report this week?"), EPS surprise analysis, and screening for upcoming earnings risk on a specific stock. For market-wide earnings calendar queries across many symbols, use get_earnings_calendar. Read-only.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Stock symbol to look up (one symbol per call). Exact-ticker match — no name or partial-ticker resolution. Lowercase and whitespace-padded input is normalized to uppercase-trimmed before forwarding. Returns the trailing up to 8 quarters of earnings for the symbol."}},"required":["symbol"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Ticker symbol the earnings event belongs to."},"year":{"type":"integer","description":"Fiscal year of the report (e.g. 2026)."},"quarter":{"type":"integer","description":"Fiscal quarter of the report (1-4)."},"eps":{"type":"object","properties":{"estimate":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Expected (estimated) EPS for the quarter. Null when no estimate is available for this quarter."},"actual":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Reported EPS for the quarter. Null for upcoming quarters (not yet reported) — pair with report.date to tell the two apart."}},"description":"Estimated and actual earnings per share for the quarter. Both sides may be null — see field docs.","required":["estimate","actual"],"additionalProperties":false},"report":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"date":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"YYYY-MM-DD report date. Present whenever the parent report block is non-null — use the parent's null/non-null state, not this field, to detect 'no scheduled event'."},"timing":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"'am' (before market) or 'pm' (after market). Null when timing is not yet known — only distinguishes before/after market, not an exact time."},"verified":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the company has confirmed the report date. False when the date is tentative (not yet company-confirmed)."}},"description":"Report scheduling — date, am/pm timing, company-verification flag. Null when upstream has no scheduled event for this quarter yet.","required":["date","timing","verified"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["symbol","year","quarter","eps","report"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Earnings entries for the requested symbol, sorted ascending by quarter (historical first, upcoming last). Empty array when the symbol resolved but upstream had no entries in its retention window, OR when the symbol failed to resolve (in which case it appears in not_found)."},"not_found":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Populated with the requested symbol (in canonical uppercase form) when upstream could not resolve it — typo, delisted, or non-equity ticker. Absent / null when the symbol resolved (even if it had zero earnings entries)."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Entries are sorted ascending — historical quarters first, most recent / upcoming quarter last. Distinguish "upcoming" from "reported" by eps.actual: null means the company has not yet reported. For "will earnings happen by date X" questions, use report.date. When report.verified is false, present the date as tentative rather than confirmed. If upstream cannot resolve the symbol (typo, delisted, non-equity), the response carries an empty results array and the symbol appears in not_found — surface that as "no data for X" rather than treating it as a tool failure. This tool does NOT return an "expected move" — pair with options data for implied-volatility-based moves."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:17a15faa0045886284f9225a24c4767b889df06539f2e5ee6a289ba3cd4ac13c","contract_hash":"sha256:fc90682e14eafe65ca60f902df042036d2a5078e3efa585268e264faf14543d8"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Earnings and fundamentals are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_earnings_results","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Earnings and fundamentals are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_equity_fundamentals":{"contract":{"name":"get_equity_fundamentals","title":null,"description":"Get today's fundamentals for one or more stock symbols — valuation ratios (PE, P/B), capitalization (market cap, shares outstanding, float), today's session OHLCV, trailing volume averages, 52-week range, dividend schedule, and company profile. For real-time quotes use get_equity_quotes; for time-series price history use get_equity_historicals.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"symbols":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"One or more stock symbols (max 10 per call). Exact-ticker match — no name or partial-ticker resolution. Lowercase and whitespace-padded input is normalized to uppercase-trimmed before forwarding."},"bounds":{"type":"string","description":"Trading session the day-level fields (open / high / low / volume / overnight_volume) are drawn from. One of 'regular' (regular trading hours), 'trading' (regular + post-market), 'extended' (pre-market + regular + post-market), '24_5' (24-hour, 5-day-trading-week). Does not affect valuation fields. overnight_volume only populates when bounds=24_5. Defaults to 'regular' when omitted."}},"required":["symbols"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Ticker symbol."},"open":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Today's opening price."},"high":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Today's high price."},"low":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Today's low price."},"volume":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Today's traded share volume."},"overnight_volume":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Overnight session share volume. Null unless bounds=24_5 was requested; treat null as 'not applicable to this session', not 'no overnight trades'."},"bounds":{"type":"string","description":"Session-bounds tag the data was computed over (e.g. '24_5' = 24-hour, 5-day-trading-week)."},"market_date":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"YYYY-MM-DD trading date the snapshot is 'as of'."},"average_volume_2_weeks":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Trailing 2-week average daily share volume."},"average_volume":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Trailing 52-week average daily share volume (the unqualified name reflects the upstream contract)."},"average_volume_30_days":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Trailing 30-day average daily share volume."},"high_52_weeks":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Highest price over the trailing 52 weeks."},"high_52_weeks_date":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"YYYY-MM-DD date the trailing-52-week high was set."},"low_52_weeks":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Lowest price over the trailing 52 weeks."},"low_52_weeks_date":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"YYYY-MM-DD date the trailing-52-week low was set."},"float":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Publicly tradable share count (excludes insider / restricted holdings)."},"market_cap":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Market capitalization in USD. Null for delisted or zero-share-outstanding instruments."},"pb_ratio":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Price-to-book ratio. Null for instruments with non-positive book value or no book-value data."},"pe_ratio":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Price-to-earnings ratio (TTM). Can be negative when earnings are negative. Null for recent IPOs or non-equity instruments."},"shares_outstanding":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Total shares outstanding."},"dividend_yield":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Trailing 12-month dividend yield as a percentage (1.85 means 1.85%). Null for non-dividend-paying instruments."},"dividend_per_share":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Most recent declared dividend amount per share. Present only for dividend-paying instruments."},"distribution_frequency":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"How often the dividend is paid (e.g. 'quarterly', 'monthly', 'annual'). Present only for dividend-paying instruments."},"payable_date":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"YYYY-MM-DD date the next dividend will be paid. Null for non-dividend stocks."},"ex_dividend_date":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"YYYY-MM-DD next ex-dividend date — buy before this date to receive the upcoming dividend. Null for non-dividend stocks."},"record_date":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"YYYY-MM-DD date of record for the next dividend. Present only for dividend-paying instruments."},"thirty_day_sec_yield":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"30-day SEC yield as a percentage (1.85 means 1.85%). Present primarily for bond funds; absent for individual stocks."},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Short company description in the caller's preferred language."},"ceo":{"type":"string","description":"Current CEO name."},"headquarters_city":{"type":"string","description":"Headquarters city."},"headquarters_state":{"type":"string","description":"Headquarters state or province."},"sector":{"type":"string","description":"Sector classification (e.g. 'Technology Services')."},"industry":{"type":"string","description":"Industry classification (e.g. 'Packaged Software')."},"num_employees":{"type":["null","integer"],"description":"Total employee count."},"year_founded":{"type":["null","integer"],"description":"Year the company was founded."},"financial_status_indicator":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Short code from the listing exchange flagging listing-deficiency status (e.g. 'CC0' = no deficiency, 'D' = deficient, 'E' = delinquent). Pair with financial_status_description for the human-readable form."},"financial_status_description":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Human-readable form of financial_status_indicator. Empty when the indicator is the 'no deficiency' value."}},"required":["symbol","open","high","low","volume","overnight_volume","bounds","market_date","average_volume_2_weeks","average_volume","average_volume_30_days","high_52_weeks","high_52_weeks_date","low_52_weeks","low_52_weeks_date","float","market_cap","pb_ratio","pe_ratio","shares_outstanding","dividend_yield","dividend_per_share","distribution_frequency","payable_date","ex_dividend_date","record_date","thirty_day_sec_yield","description","ceo","headquarters_city","headquarters_state","sector","industry","num_employees","year_founded","financial_status_indicator","financial_status_description"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"One entry per resolved symbol, in upstream order. Empty if no symbol resolved. Symbols that did not resolve (delisted, invalid, non-equity) are NOT placeholder-null'd here — they appear in not_found instead so the whole call doesn't fail."},"not_found":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Requested symbols that the upstream could not resolve (delisted, invalid, non-equity). Returned in canonical uppercase form. Absent / null when every requested symbol resolved."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Symbols that did not resolve (delisted, invalid, non-equity) appear in not_found instead of results; surface them to the user as "no data for X" rather than ignoring them. Present nulls as "not applicable" rather than zero. Pair financial_status_indicator with financial_status_description — never surface the indicator code alone."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:98b23fea8c3969f77449104b6ef38601d903131ecba7f5ddec6a2dc884c89730","contract_hash":"sha256:89eced38e5ad8ba62f127d773b19fc3cae9834e28a402e399b9517eb1be80311"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Fundamentals are explicitly outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_equity_fundamentals","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Fundamentals are explicitly outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_equity_historicals":{"contract":{"name":"get_equity_historicals","title":null,"description":"Get OHLCV bars for one or more equity symbols across an explicit time range. Use this for charting, "recent activity" questions, and backtesting. The server auto-selects an interval when one is not provided. If the bar's interpolated field is true, bar was synthesized to fill a gap and carry no new information.

Parameter rules:
- interval is optional; when omitted, the server auto-selects an interval that targets ~2,500 bars across the requested range. Provide an explicit interval only when you need a specific granularity.
- interval values are fixed; the server does NOT aggregate intermediate bars. For a custom interval (e.g. 3-minute), request the next-finer fixed interval and aggregate client-side.
- bounds defaults to 'regular' (RTH only). Use 'extended' or '24_5' only when the user explicitly asks about extended-hours activity.
- adjustment_type defaults to 'split' (split-adjusted, the right default for backtesting). Use 'none' for raw prices, 'all' for split + dividend adjustment.
- If the range would produce more bars than the upstream allows at the explicitly requested interval, narrow the range or coarsen the interval — the call is rejected before reaching upstream. The cap does not apply when interval is auto-selected.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"symbols":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"One or more stock symbols (uppercase). Up to 10 per call."},"start_time":{"type":"string","description":"Start of the range (RFC3339 UTC, e.g. '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'). Required."},"end_time":{"type":"string","description":"End of the range (RFC3339 UTC). Optional — when omitted, defaults to the current time."},"interval":{"type":"string","description":"Bar interval. Optional — when omitted, the server picks an interval that targets ~2,500 bars across the requested range. Intraday: 15second, 30second, minute, 5minute, 10minute, 30minute, hour, 4hour. Interday: day, week, month, 3month, 6month, year, 5year, 10year, 20year, 50year. Note: the 1-minute bar is named 'minute' (not '1minute')."},"bounds":{"type":"string","description":"Session bounds. One of 'regular' (RTH, default), 'extended', 'trading', '24_5', '24_7', 'hyper_trading'."},"adjustment_type":{"type":"string","description":"Corporate-action adjustment: 'none' (raw prices), 'split' (default; right for backtesting), or 'all' (split + dividend; intraday only)."}},"required":["symbols","start_time"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Ticker symbol."},"interval":{"type":"string","description":"Bar interval. Echoes the request when one was supplied; otherwise reports the server-auto-selected interval."},"bounds":{"type":"string","description":"Session bounds echoed from the request."},"bars":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"begins_at":{"type":"string","description":"Start of the bar (RFC3339 UTC). Bars are left-edge labeled."},"open_price":{"type":"string","description":"First trade price in the bar."},"close_price":{"type":"string","description":"Last trade price in the bar. NOT the official settled close; for that use get_equity_quotes closes[]."},"high_price":{"type":"string","description":"Highest trade price in the bar."},"low_price":{"type":"string","description":"Lowest trade price in the bar."},"volume":{"type":"integer","description":"Share volume in the bar. Zero for interpolated bars."},"session":{"type":"string","description":"Wire-format session: 'reg' (regular hours), 'pre' (pre-market), or 'post' (after-hours). Empty/absent when the bar's session is unknown."},"interpolated":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when the bar was synthesized to fill a gap (no trades occurred). OHLC values are forward-filled from a nearby bar; volume is zero."}},"required":["begins_at","open_price","close_price","high_price","low_price","volume"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Bars in ascending time order. Empty if no trading activity in the window."}},"required":["symbol","interval","bounds","bars"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"One entry per requested symbol that resolved upstream."},"not_found":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Requested symbols that did not resolve (delisted, invalid, or non-equity). Absent when every requested symbol resolved."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"Bars are left-edge labeled in UTC; convert to the user's timezone for presentation. Treat interpolated=true bars as gap-fill — they carry no new info and should usually be hidden in charts and ignored for analytics. close_price on the most recent bar is NOT the official settled close — use get_equity_quotes for that. For a multi-bar move, compute return from the first bar's open_price to the last bar's close_price; do not aggregate intermediate interpolated bars. When bounds='regular' the bar series covers only regular trading hours — gaps between trading sessions are not zero-filled, they are simply absent. When the request omitted interval, the 'interval' field on each result reports what the server auto-selected."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:9ababceb32decc3667ba5c3f9a2678a269f0afd142e91bd356eb2f9e9efbbcf9","contract_hash":"sha256:340962a29cb0089ca01ecde8a61950248d46bc7fa0b5f7b7328a4bd6028b5f64"},"category":"read.history","arguments":{"symbols":["{symbol}"],"start_time":"{start_time}","end_time":"{end_time}","interval":"{interval}"},"result":{"items":"data.results.0.bars","timestamp":"begins_at","open":"open_price","high":"high_price","low":"low_price","close":"close_price","volume":"volume"},"reason":"This reads timezone-labelled OHLCV bars for one requested equity symbol and time range.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"get_equity_historicals","category":"read.history","arguments":{"symbols":["{symbol}"],"start_time":"{start_time}","end_time":"{end_time}","interval":"{interval}"},"result":{"items":"data.results.0.bars","timestamp":"begins_at","open":"open_price","high":"high_price","low":"low_price","close":"close_price","volume":"volume"},"reason":"This reads timezone-labelled OHLCV bars for one requested equity symbol and time range.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"get_equity_news":{"contract":{"name":"get_equity_news","title":null,"description":"Get recent news articles for a stock, resolved by ticker symbol.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Ticker symbol to get recent news for, e.g. AAPL."},"limit":{"type":"integer","description":"Max articles to return, 1-50; values above 50 are capped to 50. Omit to 