type":"object","properties":{"fee_rate":{"type":"string","description":"Rate applied to compute this fee component, as a decimal string."},"fee":{"type":"string","description":"Dollar amount charged for this component, as a decimal string."}},"description":"Per-contract fee component.","required":["fee_rate","fee"],"additionalProperties":false},"exchange_fee":{"type":"object","properties":{"fee_rate":{"type":"string","description":"Rate applied to compute this fee component, as a decimal string."},"fee":{"type":"string","description":"Dollar amount charged for this component, as a decimal string."}},"description":"Exchange fee component.","required":["fee_rate","fee"],"additionalProperties":false},"cat_fee":{"type":"object","properties":{"fee_rate":{"type":"string","description":"Rate applied to compute this fee component, as a decimal string."},"fee":{"type":"string","description":"Dollar amount charged for this component, as a decimal string."}},"description":"Consolidated Audit Trail fee component.","required":["fee_rate","fee"],"additionalProperties":false},"gold_fee_savings":{"type":"object","properties":{"fee_saving_rate":{"type":"string","description":"Rate of the Gold fee discount applied to this order."},"fee_total_savings":{"type":"string","description":"Total dollar savings from Gold pricing on this order. Mention to the user when non-zero."}},"description":"Gold-member fee discount applied to this order. fee_total_savings is zero for non-Gold accounts.","required":["fee_saving_rate","fee_total_savings"],"additionalProperties":false},"sales_taxes":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"fee":{"type":"string","description":"Dollar amount of this sales tax line as a decimal string."},"fee_rate":{"type":"string","description":"Rate applied to compute this tax."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Internal tax-type identifier."},"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"User-facing label for this tax (e.g. 'GST'). Use this when surfacing taxes to the user."}},"required":["fee","fee_rate","type","display_name"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Applicable sales taxes. Empty for most US accounts; surface non-empty entries separately from fee components."},"is_gold":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when Gold pricing was applied to this calculation."},"total_fee":{"type":"string","description":"All-in fee the user will pay (or save, if negative due to Gold savings). Lead with this when presenting fees."}},"description":"Trading fees breakdown. Present only when chain_symbol and underlying_type were supplied. Lead with total_fee when presenting.","required":["occ_fee","or_fee","contract_fee","exchange_fee","cat_fee","gold_fee_savings","sales_taxes","is_gold","total_fee"],"additionalProperties":false},"collateral":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"account_number":{"type":"string","description":"Account the collateral applies to; echoes the request. Mask all but the last 4 digits (e.g. '••••1234') when displaying to the user."},"cash":{"type":"object","properties":{"amount":{"type":["null","string"],"description":"Change in dollar collateral if the order fills, as a decimal string — computed against the account's existing positions and working orders, not for this order alone. Zero is a valid answer when existing positions already cover the new legs. null when the position carries infinite risk (infinite=true)."},"direction":{"type":"string","description":"'debit' means buying power is held to cover the position; 'credit' means collateral is released."},"infinite":{"type":"boolean","description":"True for naked short positions with unlimited risk (e.g. naked calls). Warn the user before they proceed."}},"description":"Change in dollar collateral if the order fills.","required":["amount","direction","infinite"],"additionalProperties":false},"equities":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"instrument_id":{"type":"string","description":"UUID of the underlying equity. Pass to get_equity_quotes / get_equity_tradability when the agent needs live data on the held equity."},"instrument":{"type":"string","description":"URL of the equity instrument. Prefer instrument_id (the UUID) when calling other tools; the URL is retained for clients that consume hyperlinks."},"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Equity symbol whose shares are being held as collateral (e.g. 'AAPL')."},"quantity":{"type":"string","description":"Number of shares being held."},"direction":{"type":"string","description":"'debit' means shares are held; 'credit' means shares are released."},"uncovered_shares":{"type":"string","description":"Shares of this symbol that do NOT yet cover the option position. Non-zero means additional cover is required."}},"required":["instrument_id","instrument","symbol","quantity","direction","uncovered_shares"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Share-based collateral required by the strategy (e.g. covered calls). Empty for most orders — only short equity-covered strategies require share collateral."}},"description":"How this order changes the collateral held on the account, measured against its existing positions and working orders — a credit means collateral is released, and zero means existing positions already cover the new legs. Do NOT describe it as this order's standalone requirement or as unreliable. Present only when chain_symbol and underlying_type were supplied. Warn the user when cash.infinite=true (unlimited-risk position).","required":["account_number","cash","equities"],"additionalProperties":false}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["account_number","type","direction","quantity","legs","order_checks","option_quotes"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"This tool does NOT place the order — it returns a preview for the user to review. Reaching this tool means the user opted into the review step, so you MUST present the preview to the user (legs, type, quantity, price/stop_price, alerts, fees, collateral, quote) and get explicit confirmation before calling place_option_order (for a new order) or replace_option_order (when modifying an existing order). This holds even when order_checks is empty ({}) — empty means no broker alerts, NOT that confirmation can be skipped; the user asked to review, so let them review. Non-empty order_checks: present alertType + details verbatim and ask the user to confirm before proceeding. On user ack, call place_option_order (or replace_option_order) with the same parameters. With several legs, present each leg (pair it with its option_quotes entry by instrument_id) and then the net direction and price for the order as a whole. Use option_quotes (mark_price, bid/ask, greeks) to help judge cost. When fees is present, lead with total_fee; mention gold_fee_savings when non-zero. When collateral is present, show cash amount/direction; warn on cash.infinite=true (unlimited-risk position) or non-empty equities (share-based collateral). Echo the order type: for market/stop_market remind the user the fill price is unbounded; for stop_limit/stop_market note the order only triggers when the underlying reaches stop_price."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:eb40443e9ae8f53e16a2f5c00d25639c13042dff71aa5ee8ef2f462639b93d7e","contract_hash":"sha256:fd41026d6c8b34fdcaea4459e129813afa2b3f5f99da36d7484cd0e35239c686"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"review_option_order","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Options are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"run_scan":{"contract":{"name":"run_scan","title":null,"description":"Execute a saved scanner (also called screener) and return live market results. A scan's filters are evaluated against current market data at request time — results are real-time, not cached.

Returns the scan's title, the total number of matching instruments, a list of instrument rows (with ticker, instrument_id, type, and one cell per visible column), plus the active sort and filters. The agent should present results as a table and mention this is live data.

Parameters:
- scan_id (required) — the scan identifier from get_scans or create_scan. Returns an error if the scan does not exist or does not belong to the calling user.

Use get_scans first to discover available scan_ids if the user has not specified one.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The scan identifier to execute. Get this from get_scans or create_scan."}},"required":["scan_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"result":{"type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"Scan identifier. Stable across reads and writes."},"scan_title":{"type":"string","description":"Human-readable name of the scan."},"total_items":{"type":"integer","description":"Total instruments matching the scan's filters. May exceed len(results) when the scan's frontend_limit is hit.","minimum":-2147483648,"maximum":2147483647},"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"ticker":{"type":"string","description":"Trading symbol (e.g. AAPL). Sourced from the scan's symbol column; empty when the scan has no symbol column visible."},"instrument_id":{"type":"string","description":"Robinhood instrument UUID. Pass to other trading tools that take an instrument_id."},"instrument_type":{"type":"string","description":"Robinhood's own asset classification: EQUITY, OPTION, INDEX, CRYPTO, FUTURES_PRODUCT, FUTURES_CONTRACT, COMBO. NOT the vocabulary the asset-type filter accepts, and not translatable to it: EQUITY covers both stocks and ETFs, which that filter distinguishes. To screen on asset type, use the values listed in the asset-type filter's options from get_scanner_filter_specs, never a value copied from this field."},"columns":{"type":"object","description":"Column display name -> cell value, for every visible column in the scan's configuration. Values are raw numeric strings, not display-formatted: columns whose header contains % hold ratios (multiply by 100 before presenting), large numbers can arrive in scientific notation, and floats carry precision noise. Always format before presenting. An empty string means the datapoint is undefined for that instrument; the row still matched the filters.","additionalProperties":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["ticker","instrument_id","instrument_type","columns"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Matched instruments, in the scan's current sort order. Live at time of execution."},"sorted_by":{"type":"string","description":"Current sort column + direction in human form (e.g. "Volume desc"). Empty when no sort is configured."},"filters_applied":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Display label of the column this filter screens on, as shown in Legend (e.g. "RSI", "Market cap"). This is a user-editable label, so it is for describing the filter to the user — do NOT send it back as filter_type when re-applying filters; use filter_type_enum for that."},"filter_type_enum":{"type":"string","description":"Wire-format enum name for this filter (e.g. "FILTER_TYPE_RSI") — the value to pass as a filter's filter_type when re-sending this filter to create_scan or update_scan_filters. FILTER_TYPE_CUSTOM is the exception: such a filter is defined by its expression, so re-create it by sending the expression field to create_scan and omitting filter_type. Never send FILTER_TYPE_CUSTOM as a filter_type — it would create an empty filter. Empty only when the filter has no recognized type."},"predicate":{"type":"string","description":"Comparison operator in symbolic form (e.g. ">", "<", "BETWEEN")."},"values":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Threshold values for the predicate. Single-element for >/</=, two-element for BETWEEN, multi-element for IN_LIST/ANY_OF."},"interval":{"type":"string","description":"Time granularity for time-series filters (e.g. "1d", "1h"). Empty for snapshot filters."},"length":{"type":"integer","description":"Lookback length for filters that need one (e.g. RSI period of 14). Zero/omitted for filters that don't take a length.","minimum":-2147483648,"maximum":2147483647},"plot":{"type":"string","description":"Plot / price-field input for filters that have one (e.g. % Change uses "open" or "close" to choose changeFromOpen vs changeFromClose). Empty for filters that don't take a plot."},"expression":{"type":"string","description":"Upstream market-data expression this filter screens on. Populated for every filter, standard or custom — an enum filter type is a preset that compiles to an expression upstream. Useful for explaining precisely what the filter measures (which interval, lookback and session it uses). When re-applying a standard filter, send filter_type_enum rather than this; for a FILTER_TYPE_CUSTOM filter this expression is exactly what to send, as the expression field of a create_scan filter."}},"required":["filter_type","predicate","values"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Filters in effect when the scan was run. Always populated on create_scan / update_scan_filters responses; optional on run_scan."},"cortex_managed":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when this scan was created or modified by Cortex. Read-only via MCP tools."}},"description":"Live scan results: matched instruments, total count, and the scan's metadata.","required":["scan_id","scan_title","total_items","results","cortex_managed"],"additionalProperties":false}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["result"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"How to interpret the response:
- result.total_items is the total number of instruments matching the scan's filters. result.results may contain fewer entries if the scan's frontend_limit caps the rows — mention this to the user when total_items > len(results).
- result.results is an array of matching instruments. Each entry has:
  - ticker: trading symbol (e.g. "AAPL"). Empty when the scan does not have a Symbol/Ticker column visible — use instrument_id then.
  - instrument_id: Robinhood instrument UUID. Pass this to other trading tools that take an instrument_id.
  - instrument_type: Robinhood's own asset classification (EQUITY, OPTION, INDEX, CRYPTO, FUTURES_PRODUCT, FUTURES_CONTRACT, COMBO). EQUITY covers both stocks and ETFs. This is NOT the vocabulary the asset-type filter accepts and it is not translatable to it: to screen on asset type, use the values listed in the asset-type filter's options from get_scanner_filter_specs, never a value copied from this field.
  - columns: map of column display name -> cell value. Values are RAW numeric strings, not display-formatted; always format them before presenting. In particular: columns whose header contains "%" (e.g. "% Change") hold RATIOS, so multiply by 100 (a cell of "-0.0059" is -0.59%, not -0.0059%); large numbers can arrive in scientific notation ("1.98e+11"); floats carry precision noise ("-0.6800000000000068") and need rounding. An empty string means the datapoint is undefined for that instrument (e.g. Market cap for an ETF); the row still matched the filters.
- result.sorted_by tells you the row order (e.g. "Volume desc"). Mention it when describing the table.
- result.filters_applied lists the filters in effect — useful for confirming "this scan currently filters by RSI > 70".
- result.cortex_managed: true means the scan was created by Cortex inside Legend. Reads are fine, but update_scan_filters / update_scan_config will reject Cortex-managed scans — tell the user that if they ask to modify it.

When presenting results:
- Render as a table with ticker as the leftmost column followed by the most user-relevant columns (% Change, Volume, etc.).
- State total_items so the user knows how big the match set is.
- Note that results are live as of execution time — they will differ if run again later.
- If results is empty: tell the user the scan returned 0 matches right now. Suggest relaxing filters with update_scan_filters if they want broader results.

Error handling:
- "scan does not exist or you do not have access to it" → the scan_id is wrong or the scan belongs to a different user. Suggest get_scans to see available scans.
- Rate-limited or upstream failure → surface the error verbatim, no automatic retry."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:ca0b170ae40eee43225cd32f9483f7b485cf092e86a48b8a9708f6eaf38bd809","contract_hash":"sha256:b71bf3dc1830e7a681ac046f858316f44dc0feff009123b53560dbeb138582eb"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Scans are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"run_scan","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Scans are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"search":{"contract":{"name":"search","title":null,"description":"Resolve a natural-language query to Robinhood instruments (stocks/ETFs), crypto pairs, or market indexes. Use when the user names an asset by name (or partial name) instead of a ticker/pair/index symbol, or when you need an instrument_id / currency-pair UUID / market-index id for a downstream tool. Defaults to instrument search; pass asset_type="currency_pair" for crypto or asset_type="market_index" for indexes (SPX, NDX, DJI, etc.). Instrument results carry symbol + instrument_id (use with get_equity_quotes / get_equity_tradability / place_equity_order or any instrument_id-based tool). Crypto results carry hyphenated symbol (e.g. BTC-USD) + id — the symbol routes to crypto quote/order tools, the id routes to watchlist tools as currency_pair_ids. Market-index results carry symbol + id — pass id to index quote tools for current values, or in the index_ids array of watchlist tools.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string","description":"Natural-language search query: company name, partial name, or ticker (e.g. "apple", "tesla motors", "AAPL"). Required."},"asset_type":{"type":"string","description":"Asset category to search. Supported: "instrument" (US-listed stocks/ETFs), "currency_pair" (crypto pairs like BTC-USD), and "market_index" (e.g. SPX, NDX, DJI). Defaults to "instrument" when omitted. More categories (events, futures) will be added as their corresponding tools land."},"limit":{"type":"integer","description":"Max results to return. Defaults to 10; clamped to 20."}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"instrument_id":{"type":"string","description":"Robinhood instrument UUID. Pass to tools that take an instrument_id."},"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Ticker symbol, e.g. AAPL. Pass to tools that take a symbol (get_equity_quotes, get_equity_tradability, place_equity_order)."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Full instrument name, e.g. "Apple Inc. - Common Stock"."},"simple_name":{"type":"string","description":"Short product name shown in UI, e.g. "Apple". Omitted when upstream did not return one."}},"required":["instrument_id","symbol","name"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Matched instruments in upstream relevance order. Empty when no Robinhood-tradable instrument matches the query."},"currency_pairs":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Currency-pair UUID. Pass in the currency_pair_ids array of watchlist tools, or match against the currency_pair_id field on crypto position rows. (Use the symbol, not this id, with crypto quote/order tools.)"},"symbol":{"type":"string","description":"Canonical hyphenated symbol (e.g. 'BTC-USD'). Pass to crypto quote/order tools."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Full pair name (e.g. 'Bitcoin')."}},"required":["id","symbol","name"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Matched crypto pairs in upstream relevance order. Populated when asset_type=currency_pair; absent for instrument searches. Each entry carries the id (pass in the currency_pair_ids array of watchlist tools) and the hyp