le match — do not invent a symbol."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:1b5c32988b51b05c31fef235a9be918838e1e6f15e7948745b1ae462747b90ff","contract_hash":"sha256:59f47d228861ab23432def0c44934095eed9d7fa3d5661149f1df1911567bbaa"},"category":"read.instruments","arguments":{"query":"{query}","asset_type":"instrument"},"result":{},"reason":"This resolves a stock or ETF ticker from an equity-only natural-language query.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"search","category":"read.instruments","arguments":{"query":"{query}","asset_type":"instrument"},"result":{},"reason":"This resolves a stock or ETF ticker from an equity-only natural-language query.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"unfollow_watchlist":{"contract":{"name":"unfollow_watchlist","title":null,"description":"Stop following a Robinhood-curated list. The list itself is unchanged — it just no longer appears in the user's watchlists. Confirm with the user before calling.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"list_id":{"type":"string","description":"UUID of the Robinhood-curated list to unfollow."}},"required":["list_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"follower":{"type":["null","object"],"properties":{"list_id":{"type":"string","description":"UUID of the list that was followed."},"user_id":{"type":"string","description":"UUID of the user that followed the list (always the caller)."},"owner_type":{"type":"string","description":"Always 'robinhood' for follow_watchlist — only Robinhood-curated lists are followable."},"created_at":{"type":"string","description":"ISO 8601 timestamp when the user first followed this list. The follower endpoint is idempotent — re-following an already-followed list returns the existing record, so this timestamp may be older than 'just now'."}},"description":"The new or pre-existing follower record. Omitted for unfollow which has no response body.","required":["list_id","user_id","owner_type","created_at"],"additionalProperties":false},"list_id":{"type":"string","description":"The list this call targeted."},"action":{"type":"string","description":"'followed' or 'unfollowed'."},"status":{"type":"string","description":"'ok' when the upstream accepted the operation."}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["list_id","action","status"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"404 means the user wasn't following that list (already-clean state)."}},"required":["data","guide"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":null,"execution":null,"shape_hash":"sha256:b37d41f7753afa06211fc67687cec7a994d448a2e1bf9919beb82a67b18976e7","contract_hash":"sha256:028bc730d9f5516c3a772c8cedf0a928b993dcb66db730d46feafd57897da742"},"category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Watchlists are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[],"original":{"name":"unfollow_watchlist","category":null,"arguments":{},"result":{},"reason":"Watchlists are outside this broker profile’s scope.","warnings":[]},"edits":[]},"update_scan_config":{"contract":{"name":"update_scan_config","title":null,"description":"Change the sort order of a saved scan's results table, and/or replace its extra result columns. The scan's filters are always preserved.

Parameters:
- scan_id (required) — the scan to modify.
- sorting_column (required unless columns is provided) — display name of the column to sort by. Must match a column on the scan; the error response lists available columns when no match is found.
- sorting_direction — "asc" or "desc". Required with sorting_column.
- columns (optional) — REPLACE the scan's extra result columns (beyond the filters' own columns and the standard defaults). The scan keeps its current filters verbatim and gets a new configuration version — earlier versions are preserved. To add one column, pass the complete intended set (current columns from get_scans plus the new one). Columns display values, filters screen — to show a datapoint without restricting results, this is the tool, never a no-op filter.

Restrictions:
- Cortex-managed scans (cortex_managed: true in get_scans) are rejected.
- Omitted/empty columns means sorting-only. To remove every extra column, use create_scan with this scan's scan_id and its current filters.
- An expression matching a standard column's canonical form is saved as that standard column, canonical name included.

Returns the scan with the changes applied and fresh live results.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"The scan to modify. Get this from get_scans or create_scan. Cortex-managed scans are rejected."},"sorting_column":{"type":"string","description":"Display name of the column to sort by (e.g. "Volume", "% Change", "RSI"). Must match a column on the scan — call get_scans / run_scan first to see available columns. Required unless columns is provided."},"sorting_direction":{"type":"string","description":""asc" or "desc" (ascending or descending). Required with sorting_column."},"columns":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"display_name":{"type":"string","description":"Column header, and the column's identity: matching an existing column's name (case-insensitively) customizes that column instead of adding a duplicate, and two columns cannot share a name. A filter with non-default interval/length names its column with those parameters (e.g. a 5-minute RSI filter's column is "RSI (14, 5M)") — matching it requires that exact name; a bare "RSI" next to it adds a separate, default-parameters RSI column. Without expression, must name a standard column (e.g. "Market cap", "RSI", "Volume") — an unknown name is rejected with the full list of valid ones."},"expression":{"type":"string","description":"Raw market-data expression computing the column's value, built from get_scanner_datapoints (same language as expression filters), e.g. "optionsPutDayVolume / optionsCallDayVolume". Omit to reference a standard column by display_name alone. If the expression equals a standard column's canonical form, the column is saved as that standard column and display_name is REPLACED by its canonical name (e.g. "optionsPutDayVolume" always saves as "Total put volume")."},"visible":{"type":["null","boolean"],"description":"Whether the column shows in results. When omitted, a NEW column is visible, but a column customizing an existing filter-created column keeps that column's current visibility (some filter columns are deliberately hidden) — pass an explicit value to change it. A hidden column is still computed and saved."},"order":{"type":["null","integer"],"description":"Relative ordering among the columns passed in this call: lower comes first, columns without an order go last in the order given. The scan's standard default columns (Symbol, Name, price, Volume, ...) always come before these.","minimum":-2147483648,"maximum":2147483647}},"required":["display_name"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"REPLACE the scan's extra result columns (the ones beyond what its filters and the standard defaults contribute): the scan keeps its current filters verbatim and gets a new configuration version whose extra columns are exactly this list. To add one column, read the scan's current columns with get_scans and pass the complete intended set, carrying visible: false for any column get_scans shows as hidden (a hidden extra column re-sent without it becomes visible). Omitted or empty means sorting-only, columns untouched; to remove every extra column, use create_scan with this scan's scan_id and its current filters. Each column: display_name plus either an expression (from get_scanner_datapoints) or nothing (a standard column referenced by name, e.g. "Market cap")."}},"required":["scan_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"result":{"type":"object","properties":{"scan_id":{"type":"string","description":"Scan identifier. Stable across reads and writes."},"scan_title":{"type":"string","description":"Human-readable name of the scan."},"total_items":{"type":"integer","description":"Total instruments matching the scan's filters. May exceed len(results) when the scan's frontend_limit is hit.","minimum":-2147483648,"maximum":2147483647},"results":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"ticker":{"type":"string","description":"Trading symbol (e.g. AAPL). Sourced from the scan's symbol column; empty when the scan has no symbol column visible."},"instrument_id":{"type":"string","description":"Robinhood instrument UUID. Pass to other trading tools that take an instrument_id."},"instrument_type":{"type":"string","description":"Robinhood's own asset classification: EQUITY, OPTION, INDEX, CRYPTO, FUTURES_PRODUCT, FUTURES_CONTRACT, COMBO. NOT the vocabulary the asset-type filter accepts, and not translatable to it: EQUITY covers both stocks and ETFs, which that filter distinguishes. To screen on asset type, use the values listed in the asset-type filter's options from get_scanner_filter_specs, never a value copied from this field."},"columns":{"type":"object","description":"Column display name -> cell value, for every visible column in the scan's configuration. Values are raw numeric strings, not display-formatted: columns whose header contains % hold ratios (multiply by 100 before presenting), large numbers can arrive in scientific notation, and floats carry precision noise. Always format before presenting. An empty string means the datapoint is undefined for that instrument; the row still matched the filters.","additionalProperties":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["ticker","instrument_id","instrument_type","columns"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Matched instruments, in the scan's current sort order. Live at time of execution."},"sorted_by":{"type":"string","description":"Current sort column + direction in human form (e.g. "Volume desc"). Empty when no sort is configured."},"filters_applied":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"filter_type":{"type":"string","description":"Display label of the column this filter screens on, as shown in Legend (e.g. "RSI", "Market cap"). This is a user-editable label, so it is for describing the filter to the user — do NOT send it back as filter_type when re-applying filters; use filter_type_enum for that."},"filter_type_enum":{"type":"string","description":"Wire-format enum name for this filter (e.g. "FILTER_TYPE_RSI") — the value to pass as a filter's filter_type when re-sending this filter to create_scan or update_scan_filters. FILTER_TYPE_CUSTOM is the exception: such a filter is defined by its expression, so re-create it by sending the expression field to create_scan and omitting filter_type. Never send FILTER_TYPE_CUSTOM as a filter_type — it would create an empty filter. Empty only when the filter has no recognized type."},"predicate":{"type":"string","description":"Comparison operator in symbolic form (e.g. ">", "<", "BETWEEN")."},"values":{"type":["null","array"],"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Threshold values for the predicate. Single-element for >/</=, two-element for BETWEEN, multi-element for IN_LIST/ANY_OF."},"interval":{"type":"string","description":"Time granularity for time-series filters (e.g. "1d", "1h"). Empty for snapshot filters."},"length":{"type":"integer","description":"Lookback length for filters that need one (e.g. RSI period of 14). Zero/omitted for filters that don't take a length.","minimum":-2147483648,"maximum":2147483647},"plot":{"type":"string","description":"Plot / price-field input for filters that have one (e.g. % Change uses "open" or "close" to choose changeFromOpen vs changeFromClose). Empty for filters that don't take a plot."},"expression":{"type":"string","description":"Upstream market-data expression this filter screens on. Populated for every filter, standard or custom — an enum filter type is a preset that compiles to an expression upstream. Useful for explaining precisely what the filter measures (which interval, lookback and session it uses). When re-applying a standard filter, send filter_type_enum rather than this; for a FILTER_TYPE_CUSTOM filter this expression is exactly what to send, as the expression field of a create_scan filter."}},"required":["filter_type","predicate","values"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Filters in effect when the scan was run. Always populated on create_scan / update_scan_filters responses; optional on run_scan."},"cortex_managed":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when this scan was created or modified by Cortex. Read-only via MCP tools."}},"description":"The scan after the sort change, with fresh live results in the new order.","required":["scan_id","scan_title","total_items","results","cortex_managed"],"additionalProperties":false}},"description":"Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.","required":["result"],"additionalProperties":false},"guide":{"type":"string","description":"How to interpret the response:
- result.sorted_by — the sort in effect ("Volume desc" etc.).
